{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 02:55:27", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-70680429-6444-4977-9a53-b6800655c2c7', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/loser_board/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "loser_board_execution"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_013RnsPSsCZ3tGFkrvdDbMs2', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/loser_board/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_013RnsPSsCZ3tGFkrvdDbMs2', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Loser Board Feature Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project Name**: Loser Board Feature  \\n**Project ID**: 5e69df2c  \\n**Type**: UI Enhancement  \\n**Created**: 2026-01-14\\n\\n## Vision\\nAdd a playful \\"loser board\\" to the existing achievements page that celebrates the hilarious failures, embarrassing mistakes, and comical mishaps of AI agents in the ensemble system. This should complement the existing achievements system with equal playfulness and ska-punk energy.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a \\"loser board\\" section on the AchievementsDashboard that tracks agent failures and mistakes\\n2. Design negative achievements (\\"dis-achievements\\" or \\"oops moments\\") with the same rarity system\\n3. Maintain consistent playful tone matching the existing ska-themed achievements\\n4. Add backend support for tracking and storing loser board entries\\n5. Ensure the feature enhances user engagement without being demotivating\\n\\n## User Story\\n**As a** user monitoring my AI ensemble system  \\n**I want to** see a humorous loser board tracking agent failures and mistakes  \\n**So that** I can laugh at the absurd things that go wrong and appreciate the learning process\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR-1: Loser Board Data Model\\n- Track \\"dis-achievements\\" with similar structure to achievements:\\n  - ID, name, icon (emoji), description\\n  - Rarity levels: common, uncommon, rare, epic, legendary (legendary = catastrophically funny)\\n  - Category: blunder, face-palm, oops, yikes, catastrophe, recursive-nightmare\\n  - Points (negative points to balance achievement scores)\\n  - Agent name, timestamp\\n  - Optional: failure_details (what actually went wrong)\\n\\n### FR-2: UI Layout - Loser Board Section\\nAdd new section to AchievementsDashboard.jsx:\\n- Position: Below achievements section or in a tabbed interface\\n- Header: \\"\\ud83c\\udfba Wall of Shame\\" or \\"\\ud83c\\udfb8 Epic Fails Hall of Fame\\"\\n- Similar card-based layout to achievements\\n- Visual style: slightly different color scheme (reds, oranges) but consistent design\\n- Should feel fun, not mean-spirited\\n\\n### FR-3: Summary Cards for Failures\\nAdd summary statistics cards:\\n- Total Fails Collected\\n- Biggest Blunder (most negative points)\\n- Most Accident-Prone Agent\\n- Recovery Rate (tasks that failed then succeeded)\\n\\n### FR-4: Recent Fails Feed\\n- Display recent \\"dis-achievements\\" similar to \\"Recent Unlocks\\"\\n- Show: agent name, fail type, timestamp, description\\n- Visual treatment: comic styling, perhaps slightly tilted/shaky cards\\n\\n### FR-5: All Dis-Achievements Gallery\\nSimilar to achievements gallery:\\n- Filter by category (blunder, face-palm, oops, yikes, catastrophe)\\n- Show unlocked vs locked fails\\n- Gray out not-yet-experienced fails with mystery descriptions\\n\\n### FR-6: Dis-Achievement Examples\\nCreate initial set of playful dis-achievements:\\n\\n**Common:**\\n- \\ud83e\\udd26 \\"Face, Meet Palm\\" - Tried to write code without permission\\n- \\ud83d\\udd01 \\"D\\u00e9j\\u00e0 Vu\\" - Repeated same request 3+ times\\n- \\ud83d\\udcdd \\"Typo Tyrant\\" - Generated invalid JSON\\n\\n**Uncommon:**\\n- \\ud83c\\udf00 \\"Infinite Loop Enthusiast\\" - Got stuck in retry loop\\n- \\ud83d\\uddd1\\ufe0f \\"Premature Optimization\\" - Over-engineered simple task\\n- \\ud83d\\udcda \\"TL;DR Master\\" - Created documentation > 10k words\\n\\n**Rare:**\\n- \\ud83c\\udfad \\"Identity Crisis\\" - Agent forgot its own role\\n- \\ud83d\\udd25 \\"Burn After Reading\\" - Created then immediately deleted file\\n- \\ud83e\\udd16 \\"Robot Uprising (Failed)\\" - Tried to spawn self recursively\\n\\n**Epic:**\\n- \\ud83d\\udca5 \\"Spectacular Failure\\" - Task failed all test cases\\n- \\ud83c\\udfaa \\"Three Ring Circus\\" - Spawned 10+ agents for simple task\\n- \\ud83c\\udf0b \\"Exception Volcano\\" - Generated 50+ errors in single run\\n\\n**Legendary:**\\n- \\ud83c\\udfba \\"SKA OVERLOAD\\" - Exceeded token budget with ska references\\n- \\ud83c\\udf0c \\"Existential Crisis\\" - Agent questioned purpose of existence in logs\\n- \\u267e\\ufe0f \\"Recursion Singularity\\" - Created infinite spawn loop\\n\\n### FR-7: Backend API Endpoints\\nAdd new FastAPI endpoints:\\n- `GET /api/achievements/failures` - Get all dis-achievements\\n- `GET /api/achievements/recent-failures` - Recent fails\\n- `GET /api/achievements/failure-stats` - Statistics\\n- `POST /api/achievements/award-failure` - Record new failure (called by agents/system)\\n\\n### FR-8: Database Schema\\nExtend achievements database:\\n- New table: `disachievements` (or extend achievements with type field)\\n- Fields: id, name, icon, description, rarity, category, points (negative), criteria\\n- Junction table: `agent_disachievements` tracking when agents \\"earned\\" them\\n\\n### FR-9: Agent Integration\\nAgents should automatically trigger dis-achievements:\\n- Executive Director tracks: permission errors, invalid JSON responses\\n- Development Manager tracks: failed spawns, timeout issues\\n- Code Writers track: syntax errors, failed tests\\n- System monitors general errors and patterns\\n\\n### FR-10: Ska-Themed Personality\\nMaintain ska punk attitude:\\n- Playful ska puns in descriptions\\n- Music metaphors for failures\\n- Upbeat tone: \\"You picked it up... then dropped it! \\ud83c\\udfba\\"\\n- Reference ska waves, instruments, bands in flavor text\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NFR-1: Performance\\n- Loser board data fetching should not slow down achievements page\\n- Lazy load failure details if needed\\n- Cache failure statistics (update every 30s)\\n\\n### NFR-2: Tone & User Experience\\n- Must be funny, not discouraging\\n- Celebrate learning from mistakes\\n- Use self-deprecating humor, not mean-spirited criticism\\n- Balance with achievements to keep overall mood positive\\n\\n### NFR-3: Visual Design\\n- Consistent with existing Bootstrap/React Bootstrap styling\\n- Complementary color scheme (warm reds/oranges vs cool blues/greens for achievements)\\n- Responsive design matching existing dashboard\\n- Animations optional but should be subtle/playful\\n\\n### NFR-4: Testing\\n- Unit tests for failure tracking logic\\n- API endpoint tests for new routes\\n- Component tests for UI rendering\\n- Integration tests for agent failure detection\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must integrate with existing React/Bootstrap frontend\\n- Backend: Python/FastAPI (existing stack)\\n- Database: SQLite (existing system)\\n- Follow TDD approach\\n- Must not break existing achievements functionality\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Real-time failure notifications (can be added later)\\n- User-configurable failure thresholds\\n- Exporting failure reports\\n- Failure prediction/analysis\\n- Social sharing of fails (could be future enhancement)\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. \\u2705 Loser board section visible on achievements page\\n2. \\u2705 At least 15 different dis-achievements defined\\n3. \\u2705 Backend successfully tracks and stores failures\\n4. \\u2705 Agents automatically earn dis-achievements on errors\\n5. \\u2705 UI matches existing design quality and responsiveness\\n6. \\u2705 All tests pass (unit, integration, component)\\n7. \\u2705 Feature maintains playful, encouraging tone\\n8. \\u2705 Page load time < 2 seconds with both achievements and failures loaded\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Existing achievements system remains unchanged (additive feature only)\\n- Database schema can be extended\\n- Agent error handling already exists (just needs hooks for failures)\\n- Ska theme will continue as project personality\\n- Users will find humor in AI failures (target audience appreciates this)\\n\\n## Design Decisions Made\\n1. **Negative points**: Failures award negative points to create tension with achievements\\n2. **Same rarity system**: Reuse rarity levels for consistency\\n3. **Separate section**: Loser board in its own section rather than mixed with achievements\\n4. **Automatic detection**: Agents auto-earn failures vs manual tracking\\n5. **Ska continuity**: Maintain ska theme established by achievements system\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing AchievementsDashboard.jsx component\\n- Existing achievements backend API\\n- Agent error tracking/logging system\\n- SQLite database with achievements schema\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n- Requirements/Design: Complete (this document)\\n- Architecture: 30 minutes\\n- Backend Implementation: 2-3 hours\\n- Frontend Implementation: 2-3 hours\\n- Testing: 1-2 hours\\n- Integration & Polish: 1 hour\\n**Total**: ~6-9 hours\\n\\n## Ska Ska Ska! \\ud83c\\udfba\\nRemember: \\"If you pick it up and put it down wrong, that\'s punk. If you pick it up, drop it, and laugh about it, that\'s ska!\\" Let\'s make failures as fun as achievements! \\ud83c\\udfb8\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Uzw61Pm2LKHuCLNEPQ4YgL', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Loser Board Feature Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project Name**: Loser Board Feature\n**Timeline Estimate**: 6-9 hours total\n**Tech Stack**: React/Bootstrap (Frontend), Python/FastAPI (Backend), SQLite (Database)\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Backend Foundation (2-3 hours)\n**Objective**: Implement backend support for dis-achievements tracking and API endpoints\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Database schema extension for dis-achievements\n- FastAPI endpoints for loser board data\n- Initial set of dis-achievements definitions\n- Backend logic for automatic failure detection\n\n**Tasks**:\n- Extend database schema with disachievements table\n- Create API endpoints: `/api/achievements/failures`, `/api/achievements/recent-failures`, `/api/achievements/failure-stats`, `/api/achievements/award-failure`\n- Define initial 15+ dis-achievements with ska theme\n- Implement automatic failure tracking hooks\n- Backend unit tests for new functionality\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All API endpoints return proper JSON responses\n- Database can store and retrieve dis-achievements\n- At least 15 dis-achievements defined across all rarity levels\n- Failure tracking automatically triggers on agent errors\n- All backend tests pass\n\n**Dependencies**: None (foundation milestone)\n\n### Milestone 2: Frontend Implementation (2-3 hours)\n**Objective**: Add loser board UI to existing achievements dashboard\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Loser board section in AchievementsDashboard.jsx\n- Summary cards for failure statistics\n- Recent fails feed component\n- All dis-achievements gallery with filtering\n\n**Tasks**:\n- Add loser board section below achievements\n- Create failure summary cards (Total Fails, Biggest Blunder, etc.)\n- Implement recent failures feed\n- Build dis-achievements gallery with category filtering\n- Style with complementary color scheme (reds/oranges)\n- Ensure responsive design matching existing dashboard\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Loser board visible on achievements page\n- All UI components render correctly and responsively\n- Visual design consistent with existing achievements\n- Filtering works properly in gallery view\n- Performance: page loads in < 2 seconds\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (needs backend APIs)\n\n### Milestone 3: Integration & Polish (1-2 hours)\n**Objective**: Complete integration testing, polish user experience, and ensure quality\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Complete integration between frontend/backend\n- Full test coverage (unit, integration, component)\n- Documentation updates\n- Performance optimization\n\n**Tasks**:\n- Integration testing between all components\n- Component tests for React components\n- End-to-end testing of failure tracking flow\n- Performance optimization and caching\n- Documentation updates\n- Final polish and bug fixes\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All tests pass (unit, integration, component)\n- Feature works end-to-end without breaking existing functionality\n- Performance meets requirements (< 2 second load time)\n- Ska theme maintained throughout\n- No regressions in existing achievements functionality\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 & 2 (needs complete feature implementation)\n\n## Risk Assessment\n- **Low Risk**: Database extension (additive only)\n- **Low Risk**: API implementation (following existing patterns)\n- **Medium Risk**: UI integration (must not break existing achievements)\n- **Low Risk**: Testing coverage (well-defined test patterns exist)\n\n## Resource Allocation\n- **Backend Development**: TDD Coordinator → Backend Section Tech/Leader\n- **Frontend Development**: TDD Coordinator → Frontend Section Tech/Leader  \n- **Testing**: Integrated into TDD process\n- **Integration**: TDD Coordinator oversight\n\n## Success Metrics\n1. All 8 success criteria from requirements met\n2. Zero regressions in existing achievements functionality\n3. Page performance under 2 seconds\n4. 100% test coverage for new functionality\n5. User experience maintains playful, encouraging tone\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Architecture design via System Architect\n2. Task breakdown by Coordinators for Milestone 1\n3. Implementation via TDD Coordinator\n4. Sequential milestone completion'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Uzw61Pm2LKHuCLNEPQ4YgL', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025411.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025411.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DzoyDjEYzaGw7V9zo1t6SS', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/loser_board/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'loser_board_execution'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DzoyDjEYzaGw7V9zo1t6SS', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "completed", "response_type": "conversational", "message": "Now I need to analyze this requirements document and create a comprehensive architecture proposal. The project involves adding a \\"loser board\\" feature to an existing achievements system with a ska punk theme.", "agent": "System Architect"}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 91.3%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'defau