equirements\\n\\n### NFR1: Performance\\n- **Requirement**: Name generation performance must remain the same\\n- **Measurement**: No measurable latency increase in name generation calls\\n\\n### NFR2: Maintainability  \\n- **Requirement**: Code changes must be clean and well-documented\\n- **Measurement**: Code review passes without issues\\n\\n### NFR3: Reliability\\n- **Requirement**: Constraint must be reliably enforced\\n- **Measurement**: 100% test coverage for \\"Mega\\" exclusion scenarios\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n- **Existing Architecture**: Must work within current name generator design\\n- **Python Version**: Must be compatible with existing Python version\\n- **No Breaking Changes**: Existing API must remain unchanged\\n- **Test Framework**: Use existing test framework and patterns\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Primary Success**: No whimsical names generated contain \\"Mega\\" prefix\\n2. **Functional Success**: All existing name generation functionality works unchanged  \\n3. **Test Success**: New tests pass and validate the constraint\\n4. **Documentation Success**: Code documentation reflects the new constraint\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- The current `_BASE_NAMES` list in `name_data.py` may or may not contain \\"Mega\\" prefixed names\\n- This is a permanent constraint that should be maintained going forward\\n- No existing systems depend on \\"Mega\\" prefixed names specifically\\n- The constraint applies only to whimsical names, not to default/fallback naming\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- **Internal**: Existing name generator system in `/src/runtime/agents/naming/`\\n- **Testing**: Existing test infrastructure\\n- **Documentation**: Inline code documentation system\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Updated name_data.py**: Modified to exclude \\"Mega\\" prefixed names\\n2. **Test Coverage**: Unit tests validating \\"Mega\\" exclusion\\n3. **Documentation**: Updated docstrings and comments\\n4. **Validation Report**: Confirmation that constraint is properly enforced\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\nThe implementation should:\\n1. First audit the existing `_BASE_NAMES` list for any \\"Mega\\" prefixed entries\\n2. Remove or replace any found \\"Mega\\" names with alternative whimsical names\\n3. Add a comment in the code noting the \\"Mega\\" exclusion constraint\\n4. Create comprehensive tests to validate the constraint\\n5. Regenerate the `WHIMSICAL_NAMES` list if base names were modified\\n\\nThis is a focused, low-risk change that adds a simple constraint to existing functionality."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Hith4PGa1FXHKEGSCfukdv', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Milestone Plan: Name Generator Constraint Update\n\n## Project Overview\nUpdate the whimsical name generation system to exclude "Mega" as a prefix from all generated agent names.\n\n## Milestone 1: Analysis and Constraint Implementation\n**Objective**: Implement the "Mega" prefix exclusion constraint in the name generator system.\n\n**Duration**: 1-2 hours\n\n**Deliverables**:\n1. Updated `/src/runtime/agents/naming/name_data.py` with "Mega" exclusion\n2. Comprehensive test suite for constraint validation\n3. Updated documentation and comments\n4. Validation report confirming no "Mega" names exist\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] `_BASE_NAMES` list audited for "Mega" prefixed entries\n- [ ] Any "Mega" names removed or replaced with alternatives\n- [ ] `WHIMSICAL_NAMES` list verified to contain no "Mega" entries\n- [ ] Unit tests added that verify no generated names start with "Mega"\n- [ ] Test that generates 100+ names and validates each one\n- [ ] Code comments updated to document the constraint\n- [ ] All existing functionality remains intact\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n**Key Tasks**:\n- Code audit and modification\n- Test development and validation\n- Documentation updates\n- Integration testing\n\n## Success Metrics\n- **Primary**: 0% of generated whimsical names contain "Mega" prefix\n- **Functional**: All existing name generation APIs work unchanged\n- **Quality**: 100% test coverage for new constraint\n- **Performance**: No measurable latency increase in name generation\n\n## Risk Assessment\n**Low Risk Project**:\n- Simple constraint addition to existing system\n- No API changes or breaking modifications\n- Isolated to single module with clear boundaries\n- Comprehensive testing ensures reliability\n\n## Post-Implementation\n- Monitor name generation to ensure constraint is maintained\n- Include constraint validation in future code reviews\n- Document constraint in system architecture for future developers'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Hith4PGa1FXHKEGSCfukdv', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025533.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025533.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return e