{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 02:55:36", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-56e032bd-0a18-407a-9508-3031fdeb6852', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/question_interface_feedback/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "question_interface_feedback"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019QhiNjgpvzvqukYcB57FGo', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/question_interface_feedback/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019QhiNjgpvzvqukYcB57FGo', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Question Interface Feedback - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nBuild a question interface system that allows agents to request user input when they encounter information needs during execution, enabling more interactive and effective AI agent workflows.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Agent Question Capability**: Allow agents to pause execution and request specific information from users\\n2. **Question Management**: Store and track agent questions with full lifecycle management\\n3. **User Interface**: Provide web UI for users to view and answer pending questions\\n4. **Agent Resumption**: Resume agent execution after questions are answered\\n5. **Persistent Storage**: Maintain question history and answers for audit/reference\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- **Backend Services**: Question storage, CRUD operations, agent integration\\n- **Frontend UI**: Questions list page, answer modal, filtering capabilities\\n- **Agent Integration**: Modify agent execution to support info_needed status\\n- **Job Management**: Track job state when questions are pending\\n- **Data Models**: Question schema with validation and persistence\\n- **Testing**: Full TDD coverage with unit and integration tests\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Real-time notifications (future enhancement)\\n- Multi-user question assignment (single-user system)\\n- Question priority/urgency levels\\n- Complex question types (only text Q&A for v1)\\n- Question templates or predefined options\\n- Integration with external systems\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Functionality**: Agents can request user input and resume after answers\\n2. **Performance**: Question creation <100ms, retrieval <200ms\\n3. **Reliability**: No data loss, atomic operations, error recovery\\n4. **Usability**: Clear UI for question management and answering\\n5. **Test Coverage**: >80% backend coverage, critical path frontend tests\\n6. **Documentation**: Complete API docs, user guide, maintenance procedures\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Backend Architecture\\n- **FastAPI Framework**: RESTful API endpoints\\n- **JSON File Storage**: Questions stored in `~/.ensemble/questions/` directory\\n- **Pydantic Models**: Data validation and serialization\\n- **Service Layer**: Business logic separation from storage\\n- **Agent Integration**: Hook into existing agent execution flow\\n\\n### Frontend Architecture  \\n- **React Framework**: Component-based UI\\n- **API Client**: Service layer for backend communication\\n- **State Management**: React hooks/context for question state\\n- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-friendly interface\\n- **Component Structure**: Questions list, answer modal, filters\\n\\n### Data Schema\\n```javascript\\nQuestion {\\n  question_id: UUID4,\\n  job_id: UUID4,\\n  agent_type: string,\\n  question_text: string (max 1000 chars),\\n  context: string (max 5000 chars),\\n  status: \'pending\' | \'answered\',\\n  created_at: datetime,\\n  answered_at: datetime?,\\n  answer_text: string? (max 10000 chars),\\n  original_input_data: object\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- **Single-User System**: No authentication required\\n- **File-Based Storage**: Use JSON files (matches feedback pattern)\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Don\'t break existing agent functionality\\n- **Performance Requirements**: Fast question operations for good UX\\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful degradation, clear error messages\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\nThe project is structured in multiple milestones as defined in:\\n- `backend_tasks_m1.md` - Backend foundation and storage\\n- `frontend_tasks_m1.md` - Frontend preparation tasks\\n\\n**Milestone 1**: Backend Foundation & Storage (Critical Path)\\n**Milestone 2**: API Endpoints & Validation  \\n**Milestone 3**: Agent Integration & Job Management\\n**Milestone 4**: Frontend UI Implementation\\n**Milestone 5**: Integration Testing & Documentation\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Technology Stack**: Python/FastAPI backend, React frontend (existing system)\\n2. **Storage Pattern**: Follow feedback pattern architecture\\n3. **Agent Output Format**: Agents can return `status=\\"info_needed\\"` with question data\\n4. **Job Tracking**: Existing job state management system available\\n5. **Development Process**: TDD approach with comprehensive testing\\n6. **Single User**: No multi-user considerations needed\\n7. **Deployment**: Standard production patterns assumed\\n\\nThis requirements document was synthesized from the detailed task breakdown files to provide the missing project context."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TDgSfnHbGpzWko7oGykt3t', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Question Interface Feedback - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nBuild a question interface system that allows agents to request user input when they encounter information needs during execution, enabling more interactive and effective AI agent workflows.\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Backend Foundation & Storage (Critical Path)\n**Objective**: Establish core backend infrastructure for question management\n**Duration**: Priority milestone - critical path\n**Deliverables**:\n- Question data models with Pydantic validation\n- File-based storage system (`~/.ensemble/questions/`)\n- Basic CRUD operations for question management\n- Service layer abstraction for business logic\n- Unit tests for all components\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Questions can be stored and retrieved from JSON files\n- Data validation works correctly for all fields\n- Storage operations are atomic and handle errors gracefully\n- Test coverage >80% for all backend foundation components\n\n**Dependencies**: None (foundation milestone)\n\n### Milestone 2: API Endpoints & Validation\n**Objective**: Expose question functionality through REST API\n**Duration**: Depends on Milestone 1\n**Deliverables**:\n- FastAPI endpoints for question CRUD operations\n- Request/response models with proper validation\n- Error handling and HTTP status codes\n- API documentation with OpenAPI/Swagger\n- Integration tests for all endpoints\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All CRUD operations available via REST API\n- Proper HTTP status codes and error responses\n- API response times <100ms for creation, <200ms for retrieval\n- Complete API documentation generated\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (Backend Foundation)\n\n### Milestone 3: Agent Integration & Job Management\n**Objective**: Enable agents to request user input and pause execution\n**Duration**: Depends on Milestone 2\n**Deliverables**:\n- Agent execution hooks for info_needed status\n- Job state management for pending questions\n- Agent resumption capability after answers\n- Integration with existing agent framework\n- End-to-end workflow tests\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Agents can return info_needed status with question data\n- Job execution pauses appropriately for questions\n- Agents resume correctly after answers provided\n- No breaking changes to existing agent functionality\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (API Endpoints)\n\n### Milestone 4: Frontend UI Implementation\n**Objective**: Provide web interface for question management\n**Duration**: Can start after Milestone 2, depends on Milestone 3 for full functionality\n**Deliverables**:\n- React components for questions list and answer modal\n- API client service for backend communication\n- Responsive design for mobile/desktop\n- State management for question lifecycle\n- Frontend component tests\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Users can view all pending questions\n- Clear answer modal interface with validation\n- Questions update status correctly after answering\n- Mobile-responsive design works properly\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (API Endpoints) for development, Milestone 3 for full integration\n\n### Milestone 5: Integration Testing & Documentation\n**Objective**: Ensure complete system reliability and maintainability\n**Duration**: Depends on Milestones 1-4\n**Deliverables**:\n- End-to-end integration tests\n- Performance testing and optimization\n- User documentation and maintenance guide\n- Production deployment preparation\n- Final quality assurance\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All user workflows work end-to-end\n- Performance requirements met (creation <100ms, retrieval <200ms)\n- Complete documentation for users and maintainers\n- System ready for production deployment\n\n**Dependencies**: All previous milestones (1-4)\n\n## Critical Path Analysis\n**Primary Path**: Milestone 1 → Milestone 2 → Milestone 3 → Milestone 5\n**Parallel Work**: Milestone 4 can start after Milestone 2\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- **Backend First Approach**: Prioritize backend stability before frontend work\n- **Incremental Testing**: Test each milestone thoroughly before proceeding\n- **Agent Integration Risk**: Thorough testing to prevent breaking existing functionality\n- **Performance Monitoring**: Early performance testing in Milestone 2\n\n## Project Timeline\n**Phase 1 (Critical)**: Milestones 1-2 (Backend foundation and API)\n**Phase 2 (Integration)**: Milestone 3 (Agent integration)\n**Phase 3 (User Interface)**: Milestone 4 (Frontend implementation)\n**Phase 4 (Completion)**: Milestone 5 (Testing and documentation)\n\nThis plan ensures a solid foundation before building dependent functionality, while allowing for parallel frontend development once APIs are stable.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TDgSfnHbGpzWko7oGykt3t', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025512.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025512.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Q9FX92EJFQiZoph8ExkGtw', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/question_interface_feedback/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'question_interface_feedback'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Q9FX92EJFQiZoph8ExkGtw', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 91.3%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'c