# Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- **Backend Services**: Question storage, CRUD operations, agent integration\\n- **Frontend UI**: Questions list page, answer modal, filtering capabilities\\n- **Agent Integration**: Modify agent execution to support info_needed status\\n- **Job Management**: Track job state when questions are pending\\n- **Data Models**: Question schema with validation and persistence\\n- **Testing**: Full TDD coverage with unit and integration tests\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Real-time notifications (future enhancement)\\n- Multi-user question assignment (single-user system)\\n- Question priority/urgency levels\\n- Complex question types (only text Q&A for v1)\\n- Question templates or predefined options\\n- Integration with external systems\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Functionality**: Agents can request user input and resume after answers\\n2. **Performance**: Question creation <100ms, retrieval <200ms\\n3. **Reliability**: No data loss, atomic operations, error recovery\\n4. **Usability**: Clear UI for question management and answering\\n5. **Test Coverage**: >80% backend coverage, critical path frontend tests\\n6. **Documentation**: Complete API docs, user guide, maintenance procedures\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Backend Architecture\\n- **FastAPI Framework**: RESTful API endpoints\\n- **JSON File Storage**: Questions stored in `~/.ensemble/questions/` directory\\n- **Pydantic Models**: Data validation and serialization\\n- **Service Layer**: Business logic separation from storage\\n- **Agent Integration**: Hook into existing agent execution flow\\n\\n### Frontend Architecture  \\n- **React Framework**: Component-based UI\\n- **API Client**: Service layer for backend communication\\n- **State Management**: React hooks/context for question state\\n- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-friendly interface\\n- **Component Structure**: Questions list, answer modal, filters\\n\\n### Data Schema\\n```javascript\\nQuestion {\\n  question_id: UUID4,\\n  job_id: UUID4,\\n  agent_type: string,\\n  question_text: string (max 1000 chars),\\n  context: string (max 5000 chars),\\n  status: \'pending\' | \'answered\',\\n  created_at: datetime,\\n  answered_at: datetime?,\\n  answer_text: string? (max 10000 chars),\\n  original_input_data: object\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- **Single-User System**: No authentication required\\n- **File-Based Storage**: Use JSON files (matches feedback pattern)\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Don\'t break existing agent functionality\\n- **Performance Requirements**: Fast question operations for good UX\\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful degradation, clear error messages\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\nThe project is structured in multiple milestones as defined in:\\n- `backend_tasks_m1.md` - Backend foundation and storage\\n- `frontend_tasks_m1.md` - Frontend preparation tasks\\n\\n**Milestone 1**: Backend Foundation & Storage (Critical Path)\\n**Milestone 2**: API Endpoints & Validation  \\n**Milestone 3**: Agent Integration & Job Management\\n**Milestone 4**: Frontend UI Implementation\\n**Milestone 5**: Integration Testing & Documentation\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Technology Stack**: Python/FastAPI backend, React frontend (existing system)\\n2. **Storage Pattern**: Follow feedback pattern architecture\\n3. **Agent Output Format**: Agents can return `status=\\"info_needed\\"` with question data\\n4. **Job Tracking**: Existing job state management system available\\n5. **Development Process**: TDD approach with comprehensive testing\\n6. **Single User**: No multi-user considerations needed\\n7. **Deployment**: Standard production patterns assumed\\n\\nThis requirements document was synthesized from the detailed task breakdown files to provide the missing project context."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TDgSfnHbGpzWko7oGykt3t', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Question Interface Feedback - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nBuild a question interface system that allows agents to request user input when they encounter information needs during execution, enabling more interactive and effective AI agent workflows.\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Backend Foundation & Storage (Critical Path)\n**Objective**: Establish core backend infrastructure for question management\n**Duration**: Priority milestone - critical path\n**Deliverables**:\n- Question data models with Pydantic validation\n- File-based storage system (`~/.ensemble/questions/`)\n- Basic CRUD operations for question management\n- Service layer abstraction for business logic\n- Unit tests for all components\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Questions can be stored and retrieved from JSON files\n- Data validation works correctly for all fields\n- Storage operations are atomic and handle errors gracefully\n- Test coverage >80% for all backend foundation components\n\n**Dependencies**: None (foundation milestone)\n\n### Milestone 2: API Endpoints & Validation\n**Objective**: Expose question functionality through REST API\n**Duration**: Depends on Milestone 1\n**Deliverables**:\n- FastAPI endpoints for question CRUD operations\n- Request/response models with proper validation\n- Error handling and HTTP status codes\n- API documentation with OpenAPI/Swagger\n- Integration tests for all endpoints\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All CRUD operations available via REST API\n- Proper HTTP status codes and error responses\n- API response times <100ms for creation, <200ms for retrieval\n- Complete API documentation generated\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (Backend Foundation)\n\n### Milestone 3: Agent Integration & Job Management\n**Objective**: Enable agents to request user input and pause execution\n**Duration**: Depends on Milestone 2\n**Deliverables**:\n- Agent execution hooks for info_needed status\n- Job state management for pending questions\n- Agent resumption capability after answers\n- Integration with existing agent framework\n- End-to-end workflow tests\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Agents can return info_needed status with question data\n- Job execution pauses appropriately for questions\n- Agents resume correctly after answers provided\n- No breaking changes to existing agent functionality\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (API Endpoints)\n\n### Milestone 4: Frontend UI Implementation\n**Objective**: Provide web interface for question management\n**Duration**: Can start after Milestone 2, depends on Milestone 3 for full functionality\n**Deliverables**:\n- React components for questions list and answer modal\n- API client service for backend communication\n- Responsive design for mobile/desktop\n- State management for question lifecycle\n- Frontend component tests\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Users can view all pending questions\n- Clear answer modal interface with validation\n- Questions update status correctly after answering\n- Mobile-responsive design works properly\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (API Endpoints) for development, Milestone 3 for full integration\n\n### Milestone 5: Integration Testing & Documentation\n**Objective**: Ensure complete system reliability and maintainability\n**Duration**: Depends on Milestones 1-4\n**Deliverables**:\n- End-to-end integration tests\n- Performance testing and optimization\n- User documentation and maintenance guide\n- Production deployment preparation\n- Final quality assurance\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All user workflows work end-to-end\n- Performance requirements met (creation <100ms, retrieval <200ms)\n- Complete documentation for users and maintainers\n- System ready for production deployment\n\n**Dependencies**: All previous milestones (1-4)\n\n## Critical Path Analysis\n**Primary Path**: Milestone 1 → Milestone 2 → Milestone 3 → Milestone 5\n**Parallel Work**: Milestone 4 can start after Milestone 2\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- **Backend First Approach**: Prioritize backend stability before frontend work\n- **Incremental Testing**: Test each milestone thoroughly before proceeding\n- **Agent Integration Risk**: Thorough testing to prevent breaking existing functionality\n- **Performance Monitoring**: Early performance testing in Milestone 2\n\n## Project Timeline\n**Phase 1 (Critical)**: Milestones 1-2 (Backend foundation and API)\n**Phase 2 (Integration)**: Milestone 3 (Agent integration)\n**Phase 3 (User Interface)**: Milestone 4 (Frontend implementation)\n**Phase 4 (Completion)**: Milestone 5 (Testing and documentation)\n\nThis plan ensures a solid foundation before building dependent functionality, while allowing for parallel frontend development once APIs are stable.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TDgSfnHbGpzWko7oGykt3t', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025512.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025512.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Q9FX92EJFQiZoph8ExkGtw', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/question_interface_feedback/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'question_interface_feedback'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Q9FX92EJFQiZoph8ExkGtw', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RT84nVYYt6vbHoFsTKt8wL', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RT84nVYYt6vbHoFsTKt8wL', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Request Cleanup System Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### System Goal\\nImplement a robust, performant, and configurable request cleanup mechanism for the ActivityTracker to manage memory usage and ensure data integrity during long-running sessions.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n- **Layered Architecture** with clear separation of concerns\\n- **Strategy Pattern** for configurable cleanup policies\\n- **Thread-safe design** with concurrent access considerations\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Language and Runtime\\n- **Python 3.9+**: Leveraging modern language features\\n- **Threading**: `threading` module for concurrency\\n- **Logging**: `logging` module for comprehensive tracking\\n\\n### Core Libraries\\n- `typing`: Type hinting for robust type management\\n- `dataclasses`: For clean, immutable configuration objects\\n- `concurrent.futures`: For potential future parallel processing\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### Core Components\\n1. **CleanupManager**\\n   - Central orchestration of cleanup operations\\n   - Manages retention policies\\n   - Triggers automatic and manual cleanups\\n   - Thread-safe implementation\\n\\n2. **RequestFilter**\\n   - Handles request-based filtering\\n   - Implements efficient filtering algorithms\\n   - Supports complex multi-criteria filtering\\n\\n3. **CleanupStrategy**\\n   - Configurable cleanup policy interface\\n   - Default implementations for time-based and activity-count-based cleanup\\n   - Easily extensible for future policy types\\n\\n### Data Structures\\n- **RetentionPolicy**: Configuration for cleanup rules\\n- **CleanupMetadata**: Tracks cleanup operations metadata\\n- **ThreadSafeContainer**: Custom thread-safe data structure for activities\\n\\n## 4. Detailed Design\\n\\n### Cleanup Implementation Workflow\\n```python\\nclass CleanupManager:\\n    def clear_request(self, request_id: str):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Atomically remove all data associated with a request\\n        - Remove activities\\n        - Remove agent hierarchy\\n        - Remove agent states\\n        - Remove pending questions\\n        - Thread-safe with fine-grained locking\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        \\n    def auto_cleanup(self, retention_hours: int = 24, max_activities: int = 10000):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Automatic cleanup mechanism\\n        - Remove old completed/failed requests\\n        - Trim activity list\\n        - Configurable retention period\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n\\nclass RequestFilter:\\n    def get_agent_hierarchy(self, request_id: Optional[str] = None):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Filter agent hierarchy by request_id\\n        - Supports filtering\\n        - Handles edge cases (no match, empty request)\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Configuration Strategy\\n\\n### Configurability Layers\\n- **Default Configuration**\\n  - 24-hour retention\\n  - 10,000 max activities\\n- **Dynamic Configuration**\\n  - Runtime configuration changes\\n  - Configuration file support\\n  - Environment variable overrides\\n\\n## 6. Thread Safety Mechanisms\\n\\n### Synchronization Approach\\n- **Fine-grained locking**\\n  - `threading.Lock()` for critical sections\\n  - `RLock` for reentrant locks\\n- **Atomic operations**\\n- **Lock-free data structures** where possible\\n\\n## 7. Performance Considerations\\n\\n### Optimization Strategies\\n- Minimize lock contention\\n- Use efficient data structures\\n- Lazy deletion and cleanup\\n- Background thread for auto-cleanup\\n\\n## 8. Error Handling & Resilience\\n\\n### Error Management\\n- Comprehensive logging\\n- Graceful degradation\\n- No-crash error handling\\n- Detailed error reporting\\n\\n## 9. Monitoring & Observability\\n\\n### Tracking Mechanisms\\n- Detailed cleanup logs\\n- Performance metrics\\n- Memory usage tracking\\n- Cleanup operation statistics\\n\\n## 10. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Test Coverage\\n- Unit tests for each component\\n- Integration tests for cleanup workflows\\n- Concurrency stress tests\\n- Long-running session simulations\\n\\n## 11. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. **Performance Overhead**\\n   - Mitigation: Lazy cleanup, background processing\\n2. **Data Loss**\\n   - Mitigation: Atomic operations, extensive validation\\n3. **Concurrency Issues**\\n   - Mitigation: Fine-grained locking, thread-safe design\\n\\n## 12. Future Extensibility\\n\\n### Potential Enhancements\\n- Pluggable cleanup strategies\\n- More granular filtering\\n- Advanced retention policies\\n- Distributed cleanup for large datasets\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a comprehensive, flexible solution for request cleanup, addressing all specified requirements with a focus on performance, safety, and maintainability."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see e