{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 02:55:48", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-813550f4-2bae-47ee-b35b-eae474fa7414', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/question_interface_feedback/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "question_interface_feedback",\n  "focus": "question interface system that allows agents to request user input when they encounter information needs during execution"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UZMEvrN5PTbzNrBBiobVmv', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/question_interface_feedback/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UZMEvrN5PTbzNrBBiobVmv', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Question Interface Feedback - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nBuild a question interface system that allows agents to request user input when they encounter information needs during execution, enabling more interactive and effective AI agent workflows.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Agent Question Capability**: Allow agents to pause execution and request specific information from users\\n2. **Question Management**: Store and track agent questions with full lifecycle management\\n3. **User Interface**: Provide web UI for users to view and answer pending questions\\n4. **Agent Resumption**: Resume agent execution after questions are answered\\n5. **Persistent Storage**: Maintain question history and answers for audit/reference\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- **Backend Services**: Question storage, CRUD operations, agent integration\\n- **Frontend UI**: Questions list page, answer modal, filtering capabilities\\n- **Agent Integration**: Modify agent execution to support info_needed status\\n- **Job Management**: Track job state when questions are pending\\n- **Data Models**: Question schema with validation and persistence\\n- **Testing**: Full TDD coverage with unit and integration tests\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Real-time notifications (future enhancement)\\n- Multi-user question assignment (single-user system)\\n- Question priority/urgency levels\\n- Complex question types (only text Q&A for v1)\\n- Question templates or predefined options\\n- Integration with external systems\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Functionality**: Agents can request user input and resume after answers\\n2. **Performance**: Question creation <100ms, retrieval <200ms\\n3. **Reliability**: No data loss, atomic operations, error recovery\\n4. **Usability**: Clear UI for question management and answering\\n5. **Test Coverage**: >80% backend coverage, critical path frontend tests\\n6. **Documentation**: Complete API docs, user guide, maintenance procedures\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Backend Architecture\\n- **FastAPI Framework**: RESTful API endpoints\\n- **JSON File Storage**: Questions stored in `~/.ensemble/questions/` directory\\n- **Pydantic Models**: Data validation and serialization\\n- **Service Layer**: Business logic separation from storage\\n- **Agent Integration**: Hook into existing agent execution flow\\n\\n### Frontend Architecture  \\n- **React Framework**: Component-based UI\\n- **API Client**: Service layer for backend communication\\n- **State Management**: React hooks/context for question state\\n- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-friendly interface\\n- **Component Structure**: Questions list, answer modal, filters\\n\\n### Data Schema\\n```javascript\\nQuestion {\\n  question_id: UUID4,\\n  job_id: UUID4,\\n  agent_type: string,\\n  question_text: string (max 1000 chars),\\n  context: string (max 5000 chars),\\n  status: \'pending\' | \'answered\',\\n  created_at: datetime,\\n  answered_at: datetime?,\\n  answer_text: string? (max 10000 chars),\\n  original_input_data: object\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- **Single-User System**: No authentication required\\n- **File-Based Storage**: Use JSON files (matches feedback pattern)\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Don\'t break existing agent functionality\\n- **Performance Requirements**: Fast question operations for good UX\\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful degradation, clear error messages\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\nThe project is structured in multiple milestones as defined in:\\n- `backend_tasks_m1.md` - Backend foundation and storage\\n- `frontend_tasks_m1.md` - Frontend preparation tasks\\n\\n**Milestone 1**: Backend Foundation & Storage (Critical Path)\\n**Milestone 2**: API Endpoints & Validation  \\n**Milestone 3**: Agent Integration & Job Management\\n**Milestone 4**: Frontend UI Implementation\\n**Milestone 5**: Integration Testing & Documentation\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Technology Stack**: Python/FastAPI backend, React frontend (existing system)\\n2. **Storage Pattern**: Follow feedback pattern architecture\\n3. **Agent Output Format**: Agents can return `status=\\"info_needed\\"` with question data\\n4. **Job Tracking**: Existing job state management system available\\n5. **Development Process**: TDD approach with comprehensive testing\\n6. **Single User**: No multi-user considerations needed\\n7. **Deployment**: Standard production patterns assumed\\n\\nThis requirements document was synthesized from the detailed task breakdown files to provide the missing project context."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- Successfully analyzed requirements and designed a comprehensive architecture that addresses all core capabilities including remote sync, branch management, and error handling. The proposed event-drive...\n- The proposed architecture successfully addresses the core requirements by providing a comprehensive, flexible solution for request cleanup. The design ensures memory stability, maintains data integrit...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue']