{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 02:57:44", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-eed2bcd9-100e-4f41-a12c-2bbf5adfcb1b', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Implement whimsical agent name display in achievement toast",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VzFADy5KytxNE1yvdWYeuZ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VzFADy5KytxNE1yvdWYeuZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement Toast Customization - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A) Architecture Overview\\nThe goal is to enhance the achievement toast display to prominently feature agent whimsical names while subtly indicating agent type. This will be achieved through a targeted UI component modification within the existing design system.\\n\\n## B) Tech Stack\\n- Frontend Framework: React (existing UI framework)\\n- State Management: React Context API\\n- Styling: Styled-components for flexible, component-level styling\\n- Animation: Framer Motion for smooth toast animations\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n- React allows precise component-level modifications\\n- Styled-components enables dynamic, theme-consistent styling\\n- Framer Motion provides lightweight, performant animations\\n\\n## C) System Components\\n1. **AchievementToast Component**\\n   - Responsible for rendering the entire toast\\n   - Handles layout and styling of agent name and type\\n   - Manages display logic and animations\\n\\n2. **AgentNameDisplay Subcomponent**\\n   - Renders the whimsical agent name\\n   - Primary visual focus\\n   - Large, playful typography\\n\\n3. **AgentTypeLabel Subcomponent**\\n   - Displays agent type\\n   - Secondary, muted styling\\n   - Smaller font size and reduced visual weight\\n\\n## D) File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementToast/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 index.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AgentNameDisplay.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AgentTypeLabel.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 styles.ts\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 toastTheme.ts\\n```\\n\\n## E) Design Specifications\\n### Name Display\\n- Font: Slightly playful, rounded sans-serif\\n- Size: Larger (120-140% of base font)\\n- Color: Primary theme color with slight vibrancy\\n\\n### Type Label\\n- Font: Same family, lighter weight\\n- Size: 70-80% of name font size\\n- Color: Muted, neutral tone\\n- Positioning: Subtly placed near or below name\\n\\n## F) Implementation Strategy\\n1. Create new subcomponents for name and type display\\n2. Modify existing toast rendering logic\\n3. Use styled-components for theme-consistent styling\\n4. Ensure no changes to core achievement tracking\\n\\n## G) Interaction Flow\\n```\\nAgentMetadata -> AchievementToast -> \\n  [AgentNameDisplay, AgentTypeLabel] -> Rendered Toast\\n```\\n\\n## H) Constraints Handling\\n- No modifications to achievement tracking logic\\n- Preserves existing toast duration and animation\\n- Consistent with current color scheme via theme variables\\n\\n## I) Alternatives Considered\\n1. **Full Redesign**\\n   - Pros: Complete visual refresh\\n   - Cons: High implementation cost, potential user confusion\\n   - Verdict: Rejected in favor of incremental improvement\\n\\n2. **CSS-only Solution**\\n   - Pros: Minimal code changes\\n   - Cons: Limited styling flexibility\\n   - Verdict: Rejected; styled-components offers better control\\n\\n## J) Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: Styling breaks responsive design\\n  - **Mitigation**: Thorough testing across device sizes\\n- **Risk**: Performance impact\\n  - **Mitigation**: Lightweight components, memoization\\n\\n## K) Open Questions\\n- Confirm exact typographic preferences\\n- Validate proposed color subtlety\\n\\n## L) Testing Approach\\n- Unit tests for component rendering\\n- Snapshot testing for UI consistency\\n- Responsive design verification\\n- Accessibility compliance checks\\n\\n## Recommendations\\n1. Implement as a small, incremental UI improvement\\n2. Conduct user testing to validate visual appeal\\n3. Monitor performance and user feedback"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "