cations\\n- Styled-components enables dynamic, theme-consistent styling\\n- Framer Motion provides lightweight, performant animations\\n\\n## C) System Components\\n1. **AchievementToast Component**\\n   - Responsible for rendering the entire toast\\n   - Handles layout and styling of agent name and type\\n   - Manages display logic and animations\\n\\n2. **AgentNameDisplay Subcomponent**\\n   - Renders the whimsical agent name\\n   - Primary visual focus\\n   - Large, playful typography\\n\\n3. **AgentTypeLabel Subcomponent**\\n   - Displays agent type\\n   - Secondary, muted styling\\n   - Smaller font size and reduced visual weight\\n\\n## D) File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementToast/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 index.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AgentNameDisplay.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AgentTypeLabel.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 styles.ts\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 toastTheme.ts\\n```\\n\\n## E) Design Specifications\\n### Name Display\\n- Font: Slightly playful, rounded sans-serif\\n- Size: Larger (120-140% of base font)\\n- Color: Primary theme color with slight vibrancy\\n\\n### Type Label\\n- Font: Same family, lighter weight\\n- Size: 70-80% of name font size\\n- Color: Muted, neutral tone\\n- Positioning: Subtly placed near or below name\\n\\n## F) Implementation Strategy\\n1. Create new subcomponents for name and type display\\n2. Modify existing toast rendering logic\\n3. Use styled-components for theme-consistent styling\\n4. Ensure no changes to core achievement tracking\\n\\n## G) Interaction Flow\\n```\\nAgentMetadata -> AchievementToast -> \\n  [AgentNameDisplay, AgentTypeLabel] -> Rendered Toast\\n```\\n\\n## H) Constraints Handling\\n- No modifications to achievement tracking logic\\n- Preserves existing toast duration and animation\\n- Consistent with current color scheme via theme variables\\n\\n## I) Alternatives Considered\\n1. **Full Redesign**\\n   - Pros: Complete visual refresh\\n   - Cons: High implementation cost, potential user confusion\\n   - Verdict: Rejected in favor of incremental improvement\\n\\n2. **CSS-only Solution**\\n   - Pros: Minimal code changes\\n   - Cons: Limited styling flexibility\\n   - Verdict: Rejected; styled-components offers better control\\n\\n## J) Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: Styling breaks responsive design\\n  - **Mitigation**: Thorough testing across device sizes\\n- **Risk**: Performance impact\\n  - **Mitigation**: Lightweight components, memoization\\n\\n## K) Open Questions\\n- Confirm exact typographic preferences\\n- Validate proposed color subtlety\\n\\n## L) Testing Approach\\n- Unit tests for component rendering\\n- Snapshot testing for UI consistency\\n- Responsive design verification\\n- Accessibility compliance checks\\n\\n## Recommendations\\n1. Implement as a small, incremental UI improvement\\n2. Conduct user testing to validate visual appeal\\n3. Monitor performance and user feedback"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DEZzqzoMGQHNY4poCY71Ku', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DEZzqzoMGQHNY4poCY71Ku', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement Toast Customization Requirements\\n\\n## Objective\\nModify the achievement toast display to emphasize the agent\'s whimsical name while subtly indicating the agent type.\\n\\n## Specific Requirements\\n1. Display the full whimsical name of the agent prominently\\n2. Show agent type in a less prominent, smaller or muted format\\n3. Ensure the toast remains visually clean and easily readable\\n4. Maintain consistency with existing UI design language\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- Whimsical name is 