{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 02:58:13", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9f70d0d7-adf3-424e-b81b-e1a84090991d', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Implement whimsical agent name display in achievement toast",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VzFADy5KytxNE1yvdWYeuZ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VzFADy5KytxNE1yvdWYeuZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement Toast Customization - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A) Architecture Overview\\nThe goal is to enhance the achievement toast display to prominently feature agent whimsical names while subtly indicating agent type. This will be achieved through a targeted UI component modification within the existing design system.\\n\\n## B) Tech Stack\\n- Frontend Framework: React (existing UI framework)\\n- State Management: React Context API\\n- Styling: Styled-components for flexible, component-level styling\\n- Animation: Framer Motion for smooth toast animations\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n- React allows precise component-level modifications\\n- Styled-components enables dynamic, theme-consistent styling\\n- Framer Motion provides lightweight, performant animations\\n\\n## C) System Components\\n1. **AchievementToast Component**\\n   - Responsible for rendering the entire toast\\n   - Handles layout and styling of agent name and type\\n   - Manages display logic and animations\\n\\n2. **AgentNameDisplay Subcomponent**\\n   - Renders the whimsical agent name\\n   - Primary visual focus\\n   - Large, playful typography\\n\\n3. **AgentTypeLabel Subcomponent**\\n   - Displays agent type\\n   - Secondary, muted styling\\n   - Smaller font size and reduced visual weight\\n\\n## D) File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementToast/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 index.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AgentNameDisplay.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AgentTypeLabel.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 styles.ts\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 toastTheme.ts\\n```\\n\\n## E) Design Specifications\\n### Name Display\\n- Font: Slightly playful, rounded sans-serif\\n- Size: Larger (120-140% of base font)\\n- Color: Primary theme color with slight vibrancy\\n\\n### Type Label\\n- Font: Same family, lighter weight\\n- Size: 70-80% of name font size\\n- Color: Muted, neutral tone\\n- Positioning: Subtly placed near or below name\\n\\n## F) Implementation Strategy\\n1. Create new subcomponents for name and type display\\n2. Modify existing toast rendering logic\\n3. Use styled-components for theme-consistent styling\\n4. Ensure no changes to core achievement tracking\\n\\n## G) Interaction Flow\\n```\\nAgentMetadata -> AchievementToast -> \\n  [AgentNameDisplay, AgentTypeLabel] -> Rendered Toast\\n```\\n\\n## H) Constraints Handling\\n- No modifications to achievement tracking logic\\n- Preserves existing toast duration and animation\\n- Consistent with current color scheme via theme variables\\n\\n## I) Alternatives Considered\\n1. **Full Redesign**\\n   - Pros: Complete visual refresh\\n   - Cons: High implementation cost, potential user confusion\\n   - Verdict: Rejected in favor of incremental improvement\\n\\n2. **CSS-only Solution**\\n   - Pros: Minimal code changes\\n   - Cons: Limited styling flexibility\\n   - Verdict: Rejected; styled-components offers better control\\n\\n## J) Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: Styling breaks responsive design\\n  - **Mitigation**: Thorough testing across device sizes\\n- **Risk**: Performance impact\\n  - **Mitigation**: Lightweight components, memoization\\n\\n## K) Open Questions\\n- Confirm exact typographic preferences\\n- Validate proposed color subtlety\\n\\n## L) Testing Approach\\n- Unit tests for component rendering\\n- Snapshot testing for UI consistency\\n- Responsive design verification\\n- Accessibility compliance checks\\n\\n## Recommendations\\n1. Implement as a small, incremental UI improvement\\n2. Conduct user testing to validate visual appeal\\n3. Monitor performance and user feedback"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DEZzqzoMGQHNY4poCY71Ku', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DEZzqzoMGQHNY4poCY71Ku', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement Toast Customization Requirements\\n\\n## Objective\\nModify the achievement toast display to emphasize the agent\'s whimsical name while subtly indicating the agent type.\\n\\n## Specific Requirements\\n1. Display the full whimsical name of the agent prominently\\n2. Show agent type in a less prominent, smaller or muted format\\n3. Ensure the toast remains visually clean and easily readable\\n4. Maintain consistency with existing UI design language\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- Whimsical name is the primary focus of the achievement toast\\n- Agent type is present but not distracting\\n- Toast design feels playful and informative\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Do not modify core achievement tracking logic\\n- Maintain current toast animation and display duration\\n- Consistent with existing color scheme and design system\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Whimsical names are already stored in the agent metadata\\n- Current toast system allows for custom text styling"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FbiKEs4nGLrzWG4DLZvhLu', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': "# Frontend Tasks - Implement Whimsical Agent Name Display in Achievement Toast\n\n## Overview\nThis milestone focuses on enhancing the achievement toast UI to prominently display agent whimsical names while subtly showing agent types. The implementation will create modular, reusable components within the existing React application structure.\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Task 1: Create AgentNameDisplay Component\n**Description**: Build a focused component to render the whimsical agent name as the primary visual element in achievement toasts.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees agent whimsical name prominently displayed (120-140% of base font size)\n- Component accepts agent name as prop\n- Typography uses playful, rounded sans-serif font\n- Text color uses primary theme color with slight vibrancy\n- Component is responsive across device sizes\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**File**: `src/components/AchievementToast/AgentNameDisplay.tsx`\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Create AgentTypeLabel Component\n**Description**: Build a secondary component to display agent type information in a muted, non-distracting manner.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees agent type in smaller, muted text (70-80% of name font size)\n- Component accepts agent type as prop\n- Uses lighter font weight and neutral color tone\n- Positioned subtly below or near the agent name\n- Does not compete visually with the agent name\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**File**: `src/components/AchievementToast/AgentTypeLabel.tsx`\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Create Toast Theme Configuration\n**Description**: Establish styled-components theme variables for consistent toast styling across the application.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Developer can access consistent typography variables\n- Color scheme integrates with existing design system\n- Theme supports responsive font sizing\n- Maintains accessibility contrast ratios\n- Easy to modify for future design changes\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**File**: `src/theme/toastTheme.ts`\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Implement Toast Styling System\n**Description**: Create styled-components for the toast layout and visual design using the established theme.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Layout properly positions name and type components\n- Styling is consistent with existing UI design language\n- Responsive design works on mobile and desktop\n- Animations integrate smoothly with existing toast behavior\n- Performance impact is minimal\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3 (Toast Theme Configuration)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**File**: `src/components/AchievementToast/styles.ts`\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Integrate Components into Main AchievementToast\n**Description**: Modify the existing AchievementToast component to use the new AgentNameDisplay and AgentTypeLabel components.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User sees enhanced toast with prominent whimsical name display\n- Toast maintains existing animation and duration behavior\n- No modifications to achievement tracking logic\n- Backward compatibility with existing toast data structure\n- Clean integration without code duplication\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 (AgentNameDisplay), Task 2 (AgentTypeLabel), Task 4 (Toast Styling)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**File**: `src/components/AchievementToast/index.tsx`\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: Add Component Unit Tests\n**Description**: Create comprehensive tests for all new components to ensure reliability and prevent regressions.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- AgentNameDisplay renders correctly with various name inputs\n- AgentTypeLabel displays type information appropriately\n- Theme configuration provides expected values\n- Toast integration maintains existing functionality\n- Snapshot tests capture UI consistency\n- Tests achieve 90%+ code coverage\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2, Task 3, Task 5\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files**: \n- `src/components/AchievementToast/__tests__/AgentNameDisplay.test.tsx`\n- `src/components/AchievementToast/__tests__/AgentTypeLabel.test.tsx`\n- `src/components/AchievementToast/__tests__/index.test.tsx`\n\n---\n\n### Task 7: Implement Responsive Design Testing\n**Description**: Ensure the enhanced toast components work correctly across different screen sizes and devices.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Toast displays properly on mobile devices (320px+)\n- Desktop layout maintains visual hierarchy\n- Tablet view provides optimal reading experience\n- Font sizes scale appropriately with screen size\n- No horizontal overflow or text cutoff issues\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 5 (Main AchievementToast Integration)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Testing Focus**: Cross-device validation\n\n---\n\n### Task 8: Accessibility Compliance Verification\n**Description**: Validate that the enhanced toast meets accessibility standards and provides good user experience for all users.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Screen readers can access agent name and type information\n- Color contrast meets WCAG 2.1 AA standards\n- Focus management works correctly if toast is interactive\n- Text scaling up to 200% doesn't break layout\n- Component provides appropriate semantic markup\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 5 (Main AchievementToast Integration)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Testing Focus**: Accessibility validation\n\n## Implementation Order\n1. Task 3: Toast Theme Configuration (foundational)\n2. Task 1: AgentNameDisplay Component\n3. Task 2: AgentTypeLabel Component  \n4. Task 4: Toast Styling System\n5. Task 5: Main AchievementToast Integration\n6. Task 6: Component Unit Tests\n7. Task 7: Responsive Design Testing\n8. Task 8: Accessibility Compliance Verification\n\n## Technical Notes\n- Use React hooks for component logic\n- Leverage Framer Motion for smooth animations\n- Implement memoization for performance optimization\n- Follow existing code style and naming conventions\n- Maintain TypeScript type safety throughout\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Achievement toasts prominently display whimsical agent names\n- Agent type information is visible but secondary\n- No performance degradation in toast animations\n- User feedback indicates improved visual appeal\n- All automated tests pass consistently"}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FbiKEs4nGLrzWG4DLZvhLu', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1_20260115_025813.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1_20260115_025813.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.2\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to