{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 03:00:35", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-c2e91cd8-10a2-454d-a97a-452ca0932946', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Backend File Tracking Infrastructure - Implement efficient backend file change tracking system with file change detection API endpoint, optimized file metadata caching, last-modified timestamp tracking, and bulk file status check endpoint",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_013iKGGgQULTjN8rhYznhNxF', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_013FkhxzUP1LnVvFWXAT9A2C', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_013iKGGgQULTjN8rhYznhNxF', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble UI File Pane Stability Improvement - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\nA robust, event-driven file synchronization system designed to provide real-time file updates with minimal performance overhead and maximum reliability.\\n\\n## Technology Stack\\n- **Frontend**: React with TypeScript\\n- **State Management**: Redux for predictable state updates\\n- **Backend Communication**: Axios for API requests\\n- **File Change Detection**: Hybrid polling strategy\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. Frontend File Synchronization Module\\n- **Responsibilities**:\\n  - Manage file list state\\n  - Coordinate file update requests\\n  - Handle network resilience\\n- **Key Features**:\\n  - Exponential backoff polling mechanism\\n  - Intelligent update throttling\\n  - Optimistic UI updates\\n\\n### 2. Backend File Change Tracker\\n- **Responsibilities**:\\n  - Efficiently track file system changes\\n  - Provide optimized file list endpoint\\n  - Minimize computational overhead\\n- **Implementation**:\\n  - Lightweight file system watcher\\n  - Cached file metadata\\n  - Minimal state persistence\\n\\n## Polling Strategy Flowchart\\n```\\n[Client] \\u2192 [Request File List] \\n  \\u2193 (Exponential Backoff)\\n[Backend File Tracker]\\n  \\u2193 (Efficient Metadata Retrieval)\\n[Filtered File Changes]\\n  \\u2193 \\n[Client State Update]\\n```\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n1. Initial file list request on component mount\\n2. Periodic polling with exponential backoff\\n3. Backend provides delta updates\\n4. Frontend applies state changes\\n5. Graceful error handling and retry logic\\n\\n## Exponential Backoff Algorithm\\n- Initial poll interval: 1 second\\n- Maximum interval: 30 seconds\\n- Backoff formula: `min(initialInterval * (2 ^ attempts), maxInterval)`\\n\\n## Error Handling\\n- Network failure detection\\n- Automatic reconnection attempts\\n- User-friendly error notifications\\n- Fallback to last known state\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n- Limit polling frequency\\n- Use minimal payload size\\n- Implement client-side caching\\n- Defer updates during low visibility\\n\\n## Security\\n- Use secure, authenticated API endpoints\\n- Implement request rate limiting\\n- Validate all incoming file metadata\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n1. WebSockets (Rejected: Violates constraints)\\n2. Continuous long-polling (Rejected: High overhead)\\n3. Server-Sent Events (Considered, but complex implementation)\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: Network instability\\n  **Mitigation**: Exponential backoff, resilient state management\\n- **Risk**: High CPU usage\\n  **Mitigation**: Intelligent polling, throttling mechanisms\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n- Precise polling interval configuration\\n- Conflict resolution for simultaneous updates\\n- Handling large file system changes\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n- Unit tests for polling logic\\n- Integration tests for state management\\n- Performance benchmarks\\n- Network failure simulation tests"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_013FkhxzUP1LnVvFWXAT9A2C', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# File Pane Stability Improvement Requirements\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nThe generated files pane is experiencing stability issues, potentially due to unreliable update mechanisms like polling or websockets.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Replace current file update mechanism with a more robust solution\\n2. Ensure real-time or near-real-time file updates\\n3. Minimize performance overhead\\n4. Eliminate potential connection/synchronization issues\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Do not use WebSockets\\n- Maintain current UI/UX experience\\n- Minimize additional backend complexity\\n\\n## Proposed Solution\\nImplement a hybrid approach using:\\n- Efficient backend file change tracking\\n- Controlled, intelligent polling with exponential backoff\\n- Optimized API endpoint for file list retrieval\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- Consistent file pane updates\\n- Reduced network overhead\\n- No connection-related UI glitches\\n- Graceful handling of network interruptions"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Nw6rwpFsG3xdoGbGZ5NedJ', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - File Tracking Infrastructure (Milestone 1)\n\n## Overview\nThis milestone implements the backend file tracking infrastructure to support efficient file change detection with optimized polling. The system provides file change detection APIs, metadata caching, and bulk status checks.\n\n## Technology Decisions (Per Architecture)\n- **Framework**: FastAPI (Python) - lightweight, async-capable\n- **Caching**: In-memory cache with file metadata\n- **File Watching**: Lightweight filesystem watcher (watchdog library)\n- **API Style**: REST with JSON responses\n\n---\n\n## Task 1: File Metadata Model and Schema\n**Priority**: High (Foundation)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n### Description\nCreate the core data models for file metadata tracking including file path, size, last-modified timestamp, and content hash.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `FileMetadata` Pydantic model with fields: path, name, size, last_modified, content_hash, is_directory\n- [ ] `FileChangeEvent` model with fields: file_path, change_type (created|modified|deleted), timestamp\n- [ ] `FileListResponse` model for API responses with metadata list and server timestamp\n- [ ] All models have proper type annotations and validation\n- [ ] Unit tests for model validation\n\n### Technical Notes\n- Use Pydantic v2 for validation\n- Timestamps should be ISO 8601 format strings\n- content_hash is optional (computed lazily for performance)\n\n---\n\n## Task 2: File Metadata Cache Service\n**Priority**: High (Foundation)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: Task 1\n\n### Description\nImplement an in-memory cache service that stores file metadata and tracks changes efficiently. The cache should minimize filesystem access during polling.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `FileMetadataCache` class with singleton pattern\n- [ ] Method: `get_all_files()` - returns cached file metadata list\n- [ ] Method: `get_file(path)` - returns single file metadata\n- [ ] Method: `refresh_cache()` - scans filesystem and updates cache\n- [ ] Method: `get_changes_since(timestamp)` - returns files changed since given time\n- [ ] Cache invalidation on file changes\n- [ ] Thread-safe implementation for concurrent access\n- [ ] Unit tests for all cache operations\n\n### Technical Notes\n- Use `threading.RLock` for thread safety\n- Store change history for delta queries (configurable retention)\n- Initial implementation: scan target directory recursively\n- Exclude hidden files and common ignore patterns (.git, __pycache__, node_modules)\n\n---\n\n## Task 3: File System Watcher Service\n**Priority**: High (Foundation)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: Task 2\n\n### Description\nImplement a lightweight file system watcher that monitors the target directory and updates the cache when files change.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `FileWatcherService` class using watchdog library\n- [ ] Method: `start()` - begins watching configured directory\n- [ ] Method: `stop()` - stops watching gracefully\n- [ ] Event handlers for: file created, modified, deleted, moved\n- [ ] Automatic cache updates on file events\n- [ ] Debouncing for rapid file changes (100ms window)\n- [ ] Configurable watch directory path\n- [ ] Error handling for filesystem permission issues\n- [ ] Unit tests with mock filesystem events\n\n### Technical Notes\n- Use watchdog `Observer` with custom `FileSystemEventHandler`\n- Ignore temporary files (*.tmp, *.swp, ~*)\n- Log all file events at DEBUG level\n- Run watcher in background thread\n\n---\n\n## Task 4: File Change Detection API Endpoint\n**Priority**: High (Core Feature)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: Task 2, Task 3\n\n### Description\nImplement the primary API endpoint for retrieving file changes. Supports both full file list and delta updates based on client timestamp.\n\n### Endpoint Definition\n```\nGET /api/files\nQuery Parameters:\n  - since: ISO 8601 timestamp (optional) - returns only files changed since this time\n  - include_deleted: boolean (default: true) - include deleted file events\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Endpoint returns full file list when `since` is not provided\n- [ ] Endpoint returns only changed files when `since` is provided\n- [ ] Response includes server timestamp for next polling request\n- [ ] Response includes total file count\n- [ ] Proper HTTP status codes (200 OK, 400 Bad Request)\n- [ ] Request validation for timestamp format\n- [ ] Response time < 50ms for cached data\n- [ ] Integration tests for endpoint\n\n### Response Schema\n```json\n{\n  "files": [\n    {\n      "path": "string",\n      "name": "string",\n      "size": 12345,\n      "last_modified": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",\n      "is_directory": false\n    }\n  ],\n  "deleted": ["path/to/deleted/file"],\n  "server_timestamp": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",\n  "total_count": 42\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Task 5: Single File Status Endpoint\n**Priority**: Medium\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Dependencies**: Task 2\n\n### Description\nImplement an endpoint to check the status of a single file, useful for verifying specific file changes.\n\n### Endpoint Definition\n```\nGET /api/files/{file_path:path}\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Returns file metadata for existing files\n- [ ] Returns 404 for non-existent files\n- [ ] Proper path encoding/decoding for nested paths\n- [ ] Response includes full metadata\n- [ ] Integration tests for endpoint\n\n### Response Schema\n```json\n{\n  "path": "string",\n  "name": "string",\n  "size": 12345,\n  "last_modified": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",\n  "is_directory": false,\n  "exists": true\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Task 6: Bulk File Status Check Endpoint\n**Priority**: High (Core Feature)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: Task 2\n\n### Description\nImplement an endpoint for checking the status of multiple files in a single request, optimized for validating client-side cache.\n\n### Endpoint Definition\n```\nPOST /api/files/status\nBody: { "paths": ["file1.txt", "dir/file2.txt"] }\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Accepts list of file paths in request body\n- [ ] Returns status for each requested file\n- [ ] Handles mix of existing and non-existing files\n- [ ] Maximum 100 files per request (configurable)\n- [ ] Request validation for path list\n- [ ] Response time < 100ms for 100 files\n- [ ] Integration tests for endpoint\n\n### Response Schema\n```json\n{\n  "files": {\n    "file1.txt": {\n      "exists": true,\n      "last_modified": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",\n      "size": 12345\n    },\n    "dir/file2.txt": {\n      "exists": false\n    }\n  },\n  "server_timestamp": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Task 7: Rate Limiting Middleware\n**Priority**: Medium\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n### Description\nImplement rate limiting to prevent excessive polling from overwhelming the backend.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Rate limit: 60 requests per minute per client\n- [ ] Return 429 Too Many Requests when limit exceeded\n- [ ] Include `Retry-After` header in 429 responses\n- [ ] Configurable rate limit values\n- [ ] In-memory rate tracking (no external dependencies)\n- [ ] Unit tests for rate limiting logic\n\n### Technical Notes\n- Use sliding window algorithm\n- Identify clients by IP address (X-Forwarded-For aware)\n- Apply to /api/files/* endpoints only\n\n---\n\n## Task 8: Health Check and Metrics Endpoint\n**Priority**: Low\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Dependencies**: Task 3\n\n### Description\nImplement health check endpoint for monitoring and basic metrics about the file tracking system.\n\n### Endpoint Definition\n```\nGET /api/health\n```\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Returns service health status\n- [ ] Includes file watcher status (running/stopped)\n- [ ] Includes cache statistics (file count, last refresh)\n- [ ] Returns 200 for healthy, 503 for unhealthy\n- [ ] Response time < 10ms\n\n### Response Schema\n```json\n{\n  "status": "healthy",\n  "watcher_active": true,\n  "cache": {\n    "file_count": 42,\n    "last_refresh": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"\n  },\n  "uptime_seconds": 3600\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Task Dependencies Graph\n```\nTask 1 (Models)\n    │\n    ├──► Task 2 (Cache Service)\n    │        │\n    │        ├──► Task 3 (File Watcher)\n    │        │        │\n    │        │        └──► Task 4 (File Changes API)\n    │        │\n    │        ├──► Task 5 (Single File API)\n    │        │\n    │        └──► Task 6 (Bulk Status API)\n    │\n    └──► Task 8 (Health Check)\n\nTask 7 (Rate Limiting) - Independent\n```\n\n## Implementation Order\n1. **Phase 1 - Foundation**: Tasks 1, 7 (parallel)\n2. **Phase 2 - Core Services**: Task 2\n3. **Phase 3 - File Watching**: Task 3\n4. **Phase 4 - API Endpoints**: Tasks 4, 5, 6, 8 (parallel after Task 3)\n\n## Estimated Total Effort\n- Simple tasks (1, 5, 7, 8): 4 tasks × ~2 hours = 8 hours\n- Medium tasks (2, 3, 4, 6): 4 tasks × ~4 hours = 16 hours\n- **Total**: ~24 hours of development time\n\n## Notes for TDD Coordinator\n- All tasks should follow TDD: write tests first, then implementation\n- Use pytest with pytest-asyncio for async endpoint tests\n- Mock filesystem operations in unit tests\n- Integration tests should use temporary directories\n- Aim for >90% code coverage\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Nw6rwpFsG3xdoGbGZ5NedJ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260115_030035.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260115_030035.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-5-20251101', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.8\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
