ial backoff\\n- Optimized API endpoint for file list retrieval\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- Consistent file pane updates\\n- Reduced network overhead\\n- No connection-related UI glitches\\n- Graceful handling of network interruptions"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Gaib32HUaQz1HGDCuF2Mhe', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Ensemble UI File Pane Stability Improvement', 'description': 'Replace current file update mechanism with a robust solution using efficient backend tracking and intelligent polling to eliminate stability issues in the files pane'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Gaib32HUaQz1HGDCuF2Mhe', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "69ceb950", "message": "Created project: Ensemble UI File Pane Stability Improvement", "summary": {"project_id": "69ceb950", "project_name": "Ensemble UI File Pane Stability Improvement", "description": "Replace current file update mechanism with a robust solution using efficient backend tracking and intelligent polling to eliminate stability issues in the files pane", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-15T02:59:01.472605", "updated_at": "2026-01-15T02:59:01.472605", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-15T02:59:01.472605", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Ensemble UI File Pane Stability Improvement\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CqeeuSjyRYw4xSmTLQGncf', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '69ceb950', 'category': 'general', 'note': 'Starting project to improve file pane stability. Requirements call for replacing unstable update mechanism with hybrid approach using efficient backend tracking and intelligent polling with exponential backoff.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CqeeuSjyRYw4xSmTLQGncf', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UtUyvSvGP2PTuRv648CFhk', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# File Pane Stability Improvement - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nReplace the current unreliable file update mechanism with a robust hybrid solution using efficient backend file tracking and intelligent polling with exponential backoff.\n\n## Milestone 1: Backend File Tracking Infrastructure (Priority: High)\n**Objective**: Implement efficient backend file change tracking system\n**Deliverables**:\n- File change detection API endpoint\n- Optimized file metadata caching\n- Last-modified timestamp tracking\n- Bulk file status check endpoint\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- API endpoint returns file changes since timestamp\n- Minimal database/filesystem overhead\n- Consistent file metadata tracking\n- Response time under 100ms for typical requests\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Estimated Effort**: 3-4 days\n\n## Milestone 2: Intelligent Polling Frontend (Priority: High) \n**Objective**: Replace current update mechanism with smart polling\n**Deliverables**:\n- Exponential backoff polling strategy\n- Network interruption handling\n- Optimized state management\n- Graceful degradation for offline scenarios\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Polling frequency adapts to activity level\n- No UI glitches during network issues\n- Memory efficient state updates\n- Consistent user experience maintained\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (Backend API)\n**Estimated Effort**: 4-5 days\n\n## Milestone 3: Performance Optimization & Testing (Priority: Medium)\n**Objective**: Optimize performance and ensure reliability\n**Deliverables**:\n- Performance benchmarks\n- Load testing results  \n- Error handling refinements\n- Documentation updates\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Reduced network overhead vs current implementation\n- Handles 100+ concurrent file operations\n- Error recovery within 5 seconds\n- Complete API documentation\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 & 2\n**Estimated Effort**: 2-3 days\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Consistent file pane updates (99%+ reliability)\n- Reduced network overhead (target: 30% reduction)\n- No connection-related UI glitches\n- Network interruption recovery under 5 seconds\n\n## Total Project Timeline: 9-12 days'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UtUyvSvGP2PTuRv648CFhk', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025916.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_025916.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016YzHMLfCk2YGEE3aaVMiFx', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Ensemble UI File Pane Stability Improvement'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016YzHMLfCk2YGEE3aaVMiFx', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Comprehensive architecture proposal for Ensemble UI File Pane Stability Improvement, focusing on a robust hybrid polling strategy with efficient file synchronization", "key_decisions": ["Implement hybrid polling with exponential backoff", "Use React and Redux for frontend state management", "Create lightweight backend file change tracker", "Design resilient error handling and reconnection strategy"], "self_analysis": "The proposed architecture successfully addresses the core requirements by providing a nuanced approach to file synchronization. The design balances performance, reliability, and simplicity while adhering to the specified constraints. The exponential backoff and comprehensive error handling strategies demonstrate a thoughtful solution to potential network instabilities."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018Rc9cuA1tjdzYoXs6GyvYc', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018Rc9cuA1tjdzYoXs6GyvYc', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble UI File Pane Stability Improvement - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\nA robust, event-driven file synchronization system designed to provide real-time file updates with minimal performance overhead and maximum reliability.\\n\\n## Technology Stack\\n- **Frontend**: React with TypeScript\\n- **State Management**: Redux for predictable state updates\\n- **Backend Communication**: Axios for API requests\\n- **File Change Detection**: Hybrid polling strategy\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. Frontend File Synchronization Module\\n- **Responsibilities**:\\n  - Manage file list state\\n  - Coordinate file update requests\\n  - Handle network resilience\\n- **Key Features**:\\n  - Exponential backoff polling mechanism\\n  - Intelligent update throttling\\n  - Optimistic UI updates\\n\\n### 2. Backend File Change Tracker\\n- **Responsibilities**:\\n  - Efficiently track file system changes\\n  - Provide optimized file list endpoint\\n  - Minimize computational overhead\\n- **Implementation**:\\n  - Lightweight file system watcher\\n  - Cached file metadata\\n  - Minimal state persistence\\n\\n## Polling Strategy Flowchart\\n```\\n[Client] \\u2192 [Request File List] \\n  \\u2193 (Exponential Backoff)\\n[Backend File Tracker]\\n  \\u2193 (Efficient Metadata Retrieval)\\n[Filtered File Changes]\\n  \\u2193 \\n[Client State Update]\\n```\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n1. Initial file list request on component mount\\n2. Periodic polling with exponential backoff\\n3. Backend provides delta updates\\n4. Frontend applies state changes\\n5. Graceful error handling and retry logic\\n\\n## Exponential Backoff Algorithm\\n- Initial poll interval: 1 second\\n- Maximum interval: 30 seconds\\n- Backoff formula: `min(initialInterval * (2 ^ attempts), maxInterval)`\\n\\n## Error Handling\\n- Network failure detection\\n- Automatic reconnection attempts\\n- User-friendly error notifications\\n- Fallback to last known state\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n- Limit polling frequency\\n- Use minimal payload size\\n- Implement client-side caching\\n- Defer updates during low visibility\\n\\n## Security\\n- Use secure, authenticated API endpoints\\n- Implement request rate limiting\\n- Validate all incoming file metadata\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n1. WebSockets (Rejected: Violates constraints)\\n2. Continuous long-polling (Rejected: High overhead)\\n3. Server-Sent Events (Considered, but complex implementation)\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: Network instability\\n  **Mitigation**: Exponential backoff, resilient state management\\n- **Risk**: High CPU usage\\n  **Mitigation**: Intelligent polling, throttling mechanisms\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n- Precise polling interval configuration\\n- Conflict resolution for simultaneous updates\\n- Handling large file system changes\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n- Unit tests for polling logic\\n- Integration tests for state management\\n- Performance benchmarks\\n- Network failure simulation tests"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MGaTmr2hJfkmjVzvtcbWdM', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/backend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Backend File Tracking Infrastructure - Implement efficient backend file change tracking system with file change detection API endpoint, optimized file metadata caching, last-modified timestamp tracking, and bulk file status check endpoint', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MGaTmr2hJfkmjVzvtcbWdM', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 8, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Task 2 depends on Task 1 (Models)", "Task 3 depends on Task 2 (Cache Service)", "Task 4 depends on Tasks 2 and 3", "Task 5 depends on Task 2", "Task 6 depends on Task 2", "Task 8 depends on Task 3", "Task 7 is independent"], "message": "Created 8 backend tasks for File Tracking Infrastructure milestone. Tasks cover: file metadata models, in-memory cache service, filesystem watcher, file change detection API, single file status endpoint, bulk status check endpoint, rate limiting middleware, and health check endpoint. Implementation follows a 4-phase approach: Foundation (models, rate limiting), Core Services (cache), File Watching (watcher), and API Endpoints (all endpoints in parallel). Estimated 24 hours total development time. All tasks include acceptance criteria and are ready for TDD Coordinator implementation."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015rnUtaXJ6KAZEorh1Zq3gr', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/frontend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Intelligent Polling Frontend - Replace current update mechanism with smart polling using exponential backoff polling strategy, network interruption handling, optimized state management, and graceful degradation for offline scenarios', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015rnUtaXJ6KAZEorh1Zq3gr', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 18, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md", "dependencies": ["Task 1 (Polling Service) \\u2192 Task 2 (Redux Slice) \\u2192 Task 3 (RTK Query)", "Task 1 \\u2192 Task 4 (Container) \\u2192 Task 5 (Display) \\u2192 Task 6 (Item)", "Task 1,2 \\u2192 Task 7 (useFilePolling) \\u2192 Task 8 (useFileList)", "Task 1 \\u2192 Task 9 (Strategies) \\u2192 Task 10 (Error Handling) \\u2192 Task 11 (Offline)", "Task 5,11 \\u2192 Task 12 (Status) \\u2192 Task 13 (Virtualization)", "Task 1,2 \\u2192 Task 15 (Memory) \\u2192 Task 14 (Animations) \\u2192 Task 16 (Config) \\u2192 Task 17 (Debug)", "All tasks \\u2192 Task 18 (Integration Tests)"], "message": "Successfully broke down intelligent polling frontend milestone into 18 specific tasks organized in 5 sprints. Tasks cover core polling infrastructure, React components, custom hooks, error handling, performance optimization, and debugging tools. Critical path focuses on polling service, state management, and core UI components. Each task includes detailed acceptance criteria and complexity estimates. Ready for TDD Coordinator implementation."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
