{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 03:02:30", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a9c04a38-1c25-4a00-8995-b39c5228f327', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Backend File Tracking Infrastructure and Intelligent Polling Frontend - Comprehensive testing for backend file change tracking API endpoints, optimized caching, frontend polling with exponential backoff, state management, and network resilience",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NeERSByFLhLMPCvS6X5H75', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NeERSByFLhLMPCvS6X5H75', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# File Pane Stability Improvement - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### High-Level System Design\\nThe architecture implements a **Intelligent Polling Pattern** with backend file change tracking to replace unreliable WebSocket or basic polling mechanisms. This hybrid approach provides real-time updates while maintaining connection stability and reducing overhead.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n**Event-Driven Polling with State Synchronization**\\n- Backend maintains file change state with timestamps and checksums\\n- Frontend implements adaptive polling with exponential backoff\\n- Optimized API endpoints minimize payload and processing overhead\\n- Client-side state management ensures UI consistency\\n\\n### Rationale\\nThis approach balances real-time responsiveness with reliability. Unlike WebSockets (which can drop connections) or naive polling (which wastes resources), this design provides predictable behavior while adapting to system load and network conditions.\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **React** (assumed existing): Component-based UI with efficient re-rendering\\n- **Redux Toolkit**: State management for file list and update tracking\\n- **RTK Query**: Efficient data fetching with automatic caching and synchronization\\n- **React.useMemo/useCallback**: Performance optimization for frequent updates\\n\\n*Why React/Redux?* Provides predictable state updates crucial for file list consistency. RTK Query\'s automatic caching prevents unnecessary API calls.\\n\\n*Alternative considered:* Pure React hooks + Context API. Rejected due to complexity of managing polling state and cache invalidation.\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Node.js/Express** (assumed existing): RESTful API with file system monitoring\\n- **chokidar**: Efficient file system watching across platforms\\n- **Redis**: Optional caching layer for file metadata and change tracking\\n- **fs.promises**: Async file system operations\\n\\n*Why Node.js?* Native file system integration and event-driven architecture align perfectly with file monitoring requirements.\\n\\n*Alternative considered:* Polling-only approach without file watching. Rejected due to higher resource usage and potential delays.\\n\\n### API Design\\n- **REST**: Stateless, cacheable, simple to debug\\n- **JSON**: Lightweight payload format\\n- **ETags**: HTTP-based caching and change detection\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n\\n#### FileListContainer\\n- **Responsibility**: Manages polling lifecycle and file list state\\n- **Interactions**: Dispatches RTK Query hooks, manages polling intervals\\n- **State**: Current file list, last update timestamp, polling status\\n\\n#### FileListDisplay\\n- **Responsibility**: Pure presentation of file list\\n- **Interactions**: Receives file data from container, handles user actions\\n- **Optimizations**: React.memo to prevent unnecessary re-renders\\n\\n#### FilePollingService\\n- **Responsibility**: Adaptive polling logic with exponential backoff\\n- **Interactions**: Calls API endpoints, manages timing strategies\\n- **Features**: Network error handling, automatic retry logic\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n\\n#### FileWatcher\\n```\\nFileWatcher\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 monitors file system changes (chokidar)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 maintains change timestamps\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 calculates file checksums for integrity\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 triggers cache invalidation\\n```\\n\\n#### FileListAPI\\n```\\nFileListAPI\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 GET /api/files/list?since=timestamp\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 GET /api/files/changes?etag=value\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 provides optimized file metadata\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 handles conditional requests (304 Not Modified)\\n```\\n\\n#### ChangeTracker\\n```\\nChangeTracker\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 stores file change events\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 maintains ETag/timestamp mappings\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 provides incremental update data\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 cleans up old change records\\n```\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow\\n\\n```\\n[File System] -> [FileWatcher] -> [ChangeTracker] -> [Redis Cache]\\n                                                          |\\n[FileListDisplay] <- [FileListContainer] <- [FilePollingService] <- [FileListAPI]\\n```\\n\\n### Update Sequence\\n1. User action or file system change occurs\\n2. FileWatcher detects change and updates ChangeTracker\\n3. ChangeTracker invalidates relevant cache entries\\n4. FilePollingService makes conditional API request\\n5. API returns changed files or 304 Not Modified\\n6. FileListContainer updates Redux state\\n7. FileListDisplay re-renders with new data\\n\\n## 5. File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileList/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileListContainer.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileListDisplay.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileListItem.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 common/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 filePollingService.js\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 fileAPI.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 errorHandling.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 store/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 slices/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileListSlice.js\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 api/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileListAPI.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useFilePolling.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useFileList.js\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 pollingStrategies.js\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileHelpers.js\\n\\nbackend/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 routes/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 files.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileWatcher.js\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ChangeTracker.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 FileSystemService.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 middleware/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 caching.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 etag.js\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileHelpers.js\\n```\\n\\n## 6. Data Model\\n\\n### Frontend State (Redux)\\n```typescript\\ninterface FileListState {\\n  files: FileItem[]\\n  lastUpdated: timestamp\\n  pollingStatus: \'idle\' | \'polling\' | \'error\'\\n  errorMessage: string | null\\n}\\n\\ninterface FileItem {\\n  id: string\\n  name: string\\n  path: string\\n  modifiedAt: timestamp\\n  size: number\\n  type: \'file\' | \'directory\'\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Backend Data Structures\\n```typescript\\ninterface FileChange {\\n  id: string\\n  timestamp: number\\n  type: \'created\' | \'modified\' | \'deleted\'\\n  file: FileMetadata\\n}\\n\\ninterface FileMetadata {\\n  path: string\\n  name: string\\n  size: number\\n  modifiedAt: number\\n  checksum: string\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 7. API Design\\n\\n### Endpoints\\n\\n#### GET /api/files/list\\n**Purpose**: Retrieve current file list with optional filtering\\n```\\nQuery Parameters:\\n- since: timestamp (optional) - only files changed after this time\\n- etag: string (optional) - for conditional requests\\n\\nResponse:\\n{\\n  \\"files\\": FileItem[],\\n  \\"timestamp\\": number,\\n  \\"etag\\": string\\n}\\n\\nStatus Codes:\\n- 200: Success with data\\n- 304: Not Modified (when using etag)\\n- 500: Server error\\n```\\n\\n#### GET /api/files/changes\\n**Purpose**: Get incremental changes since last request\\n```\\nQuery Parameters:\\n- since: timestamp (required) - last known timestamp\\n- etag: string (optional) - for cache validation\\n\\nResponse:\\n{\\n  \\"changes\\": FileChange[],\\n  \\"timestamp\\": number,\\n  \\"etag\\": string,\\n  \\"hasMore\\": boolean\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Authentication\\nAssumes existing authentication middleware is in place. All endpoints should require valid session/token.\\n\\n## 8. Polling Strategy\\n\\n### Adaptive Polling Algorithm\\n```javascript\\n// Base intervals in milliseconds\\nconst INTERVALS = {\\n  ACTIVE: 1000,      // When recent changes detected\\n  NORMAL: 5000,      // Regular polling\\n  IDLE: 15000,       // When no changes for extended time\\n  ERROR: 30000       // After errors (with exponential backoff)\\n}\\n\\n// Backoff strategy\\nfunction calculateDelay(errorCount) {\\n  return Math.min(INTERVALS.ERROR * Math.pow(2, errorCount), 300000) // Max 5 min\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Polling State Machine\\n1. **Active**: Recent file changes detected, poll every 1s\\n2. **Normal**: No recent changes, poll every 5s\\n3. **Idle**: No changes for 5+ minutes, poll every 15s\\n4. **Error**: Network/server issues, exponential backoff\\n\\n## 9. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n```javascript\\n// config/polling.js\\nmodule.exports = {\\n  development: {\\n    pollingInterval: 2000,\\n    fileWatchDebounce: 100,\\n    cacheEnabled: false\\n  },\\n  production: {\\n    pollingInterval: 5000,\\n    fileWatchDebounce: 300,\\n    cacheEnabled: true,\\n    redisUrl: process.env.REDIS_URL\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### CI/CD Considerations\\n- **Feature Flags**: Gradual rollout of new polling mechanism\\n- **Monitoring**: Track polling frequency, error rates, cache hit ratios\\n- **Rollback Plan**: Ability to revert to previous file update mechanism\\n\\n### Docker Configuration\\n```dockerfile\\n# Add to existing Dockerfile\\nCOPY src/services/filePolling* ./src/services/\\nCOPY backend/services/File* ./backend/services/\\nENV POLLING_STRATEGY=adaptive\\nENV FILE_WATCH_ENABLED=true\\n```\\n\\n## 10. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n**Frontend**:\\n- FilePollingService logic and timing\\n- Redux slice reducers and actions\\n- Component rendering with different file states\\n\\n**Backend**:\\n- FileWatcher event handling\\n- ChangeTracker data integrity\\n- API endpoint responses and caching\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- End-to-end file change propagation\\n- Polling behavior under various network conditions\\n- Cache invalidation scenarios\\n- Error recovery and backoff strategies\\n\\n### Performance Testing\\n- Polling frequency under high file change volumes\\n- Memory usage with large file lists\\n- API response times with incremental updates\\n\\n### Test Files Structure\\n```\\ntests/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 unit/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 filePollingService.test.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 fileListSlice.test.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 FileWatcher.test.js\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ChangeTracker.test.js\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 fileAPI.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 integration/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 fileUpdateFlow.test.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 pollingBehavior.test.js\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 performance/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 pollingLoad.test.js\\n```\\n\\n## 11. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### WebSocket Approach\\n**Pros**: True real-time updates, minimal client logic\\n**Cons**: Connection reliability issues, more complex error handling\\n**Verdict**: Rejected due to explicit constraint against WebSockets\\n\\n### Server-Sent Events (SSE)\\n**Pros**: Simpler than WebSockets, automatic reconnection\\n**Cons**: Limited browser support, connection overhead\\n**Verdict**: Considered but polling provides better control over update frequency\\n\\n### Basic Polling\\n**Pros**: Simple implementation, predictable behavior\\n**Cons**: Inefficient network usage, fixed update intervals\\n**Verdict**: Enhanced with intelligent/adaptive polling for better performance\\n\\n### File System Notifications + Long Polling\\n**Pros**: Immediate updates, efficient for sparse changes\\n**Cons**: Complex state management, potential timeout issues\\n**Verdict**: Complexity outweighs benefits for this use case\\n\\n## 12. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk: Polling Overhead\\n**Mitigation**: Adaptive intervals, conditional requests (ETags), efficient payloads\\n\\n### Risk: Cache Inconsistency\\n**Mitigation**: Checksum-based integrity checking, atomic cache updates\\n\\n### Risk: Network Interruption\\n**Mitigation**: Exponential backoff, automatic retry logic, graceful degradation\\n\\n### Risk: File System Overload\\n**Mitigation**: Debounced file watching, batched change notifications\\n\\n### Risk: Memory Leaks\\n**Mitigation**: Cleanup polling timers on unmount, bounded cache sizes\\n\\n## 13. Open Questions\\n\\n### User Preferences Needed:\\n1. **Polling Frequency**: Balance between responsiveness and resource usage\\n   - Conservative (5-15s intervals) vs Aggressive (1-3s intervals)\\n\\n2. **Error Recovery**: How aggressively to retry after errors\\n   - Quick recovery vs Patient backoff\\n\\n3. **Cache Strategy**: Local storage vs memory-only for file state\\n   - Persistence across page refreshes vs Simplified state management\\n\\n4. **Update Granularity**: Full file list vs incremental changes\\n   - Simpler implementation vs Network efficiency\\n\\n### Technical Decisions Requiring Input:\\n- Should we persist polling state across browser sessions?\\n- What level of file change detail should be exposed to UI?\\n- Should polling pause when tab is not visible?\\n\\n## 14. Performance Considerations\\n\\n### Frontend Optimization\\n- **React.memo**: Prevent unnecessary component re-renders\\n- **Virtualization**: For large file lists (1000+ files)\\n- **Debounced Filtering**: Smooth search/filter interactions\\n- **Background Tab Handling**: Reduce polling when tab inactive\\n\\n### Backend Optimization\\n- **Change Batching**: Group multiple file changes in single API response\\n- **Compression**: Gzip API responses for large file lists\\n- **Index Optimization**: Fast file lookups by path/timestamp\\n- **Connection Pooling**: Efficient database connections for change tracking\\n\\n## 15. Monitoring and Observability\\n\\n### Metrics to Track\\n- Average polling interval\\n- API response times\\n- Cache hit/miss ratios\\n- File change detection latency\\n- Error rates by type\\n\\n### Logging Strategy\\n```javascript\\n// Example logging points\\nlogger.info(\'Polling cycle started\', { interval, timestamp })\\nlogger.warn(\'Network error during polling\', { error, retryCount })\\nlogger.debug(\'File changes detected\', { fileCount, changes })\\n```\\n\\n### Alerts\\n- High error rates in polling\\n- Unusual file change volumes\\n- API performance degradation\\n- Cache invalidation failures\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, maintainable solution for file pane stability while meeting all specified constraints and success criteria."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MKbLTfBAbQDDKeKL6swfYD', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MKbLTfBAbQDDKeKL6swfYD', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Fidget Spinner Achievements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nAdd 10 new achievements to the existing ensemble agent achievement system with a \\"fidget spinner\\" theme. These achievements will complement the existing categories (ska, brass_band, drum_corps, guitar_hero) with fidget spinner-themed accomplishments.\\n\\n## Context\\nThe ensemble system currently has a comprehensive achievement system in `/src/runtime/agents/achievements.py` with multiple categories and rarity levels. The system tracks agent performance and awards achievements based on various triggers and conditions.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Goal\\nAdd 10 new achievements with \\"fidget spinner\\" theme to the `ACHIEVEMENTS` list in the achievements system.\\n\\n### Specific Requirements\\n\\n1. **Achievement Category**: Create new `FIDGET_SPINNER = \\"fidget_spinner\\"` category in `AchievementCategory` enum\\n2. **Theme Consistency**: All achievements should relate to fidget spinner concepts:\\n   - Spinning/rotation mechanics\\n   - Stress relief/focus\\n   - Bearing smoothness\\n   - Trick moves\\n   - Collection aspects\\n   - Fidgeting behavior\\n\\n3. **Achievement Distribution**:\\n   - 3 Common achievements (10-15 points)\\n   - 4 Uncommon achievements (20-35 points)  \\n   - 2 Rare achievements (40-60 points)\\n   - 1 Epic achievement (70-100 points)\\n\\n4. **Technical Requirements**:\\n   - Follow existing `Achievement` dataclass structure\\n   - Include appropriate emoji icons\\n   - Define meaningful trigger conditions\\n   - Use existing agent classes or \\"*\\" for all agents\\n   - Follow naming conventions from existing achievements\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Add 10 fidget spinner themed achievements\\n- Add new achievement category enum value\\n- Integrate with existing achievement tracking system\\n- Use appropriate emoji icons and point values\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n- Changes to achievement tracking logic\\n- UI modifications for displaying achievements\\n- Database schema changes\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- 10 new fidget spinner achievements added to system\\n- New category properly integrated\\n- Achievements follow existing patterns and conventions\\n- Code maintains existing style and structure\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Must not break existing achievement system\\n- Must follow existing code style and patterns\\n- Must use realistic trigger conditions that can actually occur\\n- Must maintain thematic consistency with fidget spinner concepts\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Existing achievement system is functioning properly\\n- Achievement tracking triggers are working as expected\\n- No changes needed to database schema\\n- Standard deployment and testing processes apply"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Sf2exEE9iFYeGjgxUw4MFn', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy: Backend File Tracking and Intelligent Polling\n\n## Test Coverage Overview\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 80%\n- **Integration Test Coverage**: 90%\n- **E2E Test Coverage**: Critical user flows\n\n## Backend Test Tasks\n\n### FileWatcher Service Tests\n1. **Unit Tests**:\n   - Verify file system change detection\n   - Test checksum generation accuracy\n   - Validate timestamp tracking\n   - Handle edge cases (file rename, permission changes)\n\n2. **Integration Tests**:\n   - Verify file change events propagation\n   - Test interaction with ChangeTracker\n   - Validate cache invalidation triggers\n   - Performance testing with large file sets\n\n### ChangeTracker Service Tests\n1. **Unit Tests**:\n   - Test change event storage\n   - Validate ETag generation\n   - Check timestamp-based filtering\n   - Verify cleanup of old change records\n\n2. **Integration Tests**:\n   - Test synchronization with FileWatcher\n   - Validate incremental update generation\n   - Check cache consistency\n   - Error handling during high-frequency changes\n\n### FileListAPI Endpoint Tests\n1. **Unit Tests**:\n   - Validate GET /api/files/list endpoint\n   - Test conditional request handling (304 Not Modified)\n   - Verify query parameter processing\n   - Check response payload structure\n\n2. **Integration Tests**:\n   - End-to-end file list retrieval\n   - Test with various file system states\n   - Verify authentication and authorization\n   - Performance and load testing\n\n## Frontend Test Tasks\n\n### FilePollingService Tests\n1. **Unit Tests**:\n   - Validate adaptive polling logic\n   - Test exponential backoff algorithm\n   - Verify interval calculations\n   - Error state management\n\n2. **Integration Tests**:\n   - Polling behavior under different network conditions\n   - State synchronization\n   - Error recovery mechanisms\n\n### Redux Slice Tests\n1. **Unit Tests**:\n   - Test fileListSlice reducers\n   - Validate state updates\n   - Check action creator behaviors\n   - Error state management\n\n### React Component Tests\n1. **Unit Tests**:\n   - FileListContainer rendering\n   - FileListDisplay rendering\n   - Interaction with polling service\n   - State management\n\n2. **Integration Tests**:\n   - Component interaction\n   - State propagation\n   - Rendering with different file list states\n\n## End-to-End Test Scenarios\n1. **File Change Detection**\n   - Create, modify, delete files\n   - Verify UI updates\n   - Check polling interval adaptation\n\n2. **Network Resilience**\n   - Simulate network interruptions\n   - Test error recovery\n   - Validate exponential backoff\n\n3. **Performance Scenarios**\n   - Large file system with frequent changes\n   - Slow network conditions\n   - High-latency environments\n\n## Performance and Load Testing\n1. File list retrieval under load\n2. Polling frequency impact\n3. Memory usage tracking\n4. Cache efficiency measurement\n\n## Security Testing\n1. Authentication verification\n2. Authorization checks\n3. Payload validation\n4. Rate limiting\n\n## Recommended Testing Tools\n- **Backend**: Jest, Supertest\n- **Frontend**: React Testing Library, Jest\n- **E2E**: Playwright\n- **Performance**: Artillery, k6\n\n## Test Environment Configuration\n- Develop mock file systems\n- Simulate various network conditions\n- Create reproducible test scenarios\n- Implement comprehensive logging\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n1. **Polling Overhead**\n   - Implement adaptive intervals\n   - Add circuit breakers\n   - Monitor resource consumption\n\n2. **Cache Inconsistency**\n   - Use checksums for validation\n   - Implement atomic updates\n   - Add extensive logging\n\n3. **Network Interruptions**\n   - Design robust retry mechanisms\n   - Implement graceful degradation\n   - Provide clear user feedback\n\n## Test Execution Strategy\n1. Run unit tests on every commit\n2. Integration tests in staging\n3. E2E tests before release\n4. Continuous performance monitoring\n\n## Reporting and Metrics\n- Code coverage reports\n- Performance benchmark results\n- Error rate tracking\n- Polling efficiency metrics'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Sf2exEE9iFYeGjgxUw4MFn', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260115_030230.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260115_030230.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.7\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['a