{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 03:02:38", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-427a420a-2b88-4279-be83-12e1d0c17ad9', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Fidget Spinner Achievements"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019doSqHu4rH4LjUskBjw9FM', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019doSqHu4rH4LjUskBjw9FM', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Famous Mustards Achievements - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nAdd 10 new achievements from the category \\"famous mustards\\" to the existing achievement system in the ensemble project.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a new achievement category `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS` in the existing system\\n2. Design 10 thematic achievements based on famous mustard varieties and mustard-related concepts\\n3. Integrate these achievements into the existing achievement tracking system\\n4. Ensure achievements follow the established pattern and quality standards\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Add `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS` to the `AchievementCategory` enum\\n- Create 10 new achievement definitions with:\\n  - Unique IDs related to mustard themes\\n  - Creative names referencing famous mustard types/brands\\n  - Descriptive text that ties mustard concepts to agent behaviors\\n  - Appropriate rarity levels (mix of common to legendary)\\n  - Relevant icons (mustard/food related emojis)\\n  - Point values consistent with existing system\\n  - Trigger conditions that make sense in context\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Modifying the achievement tracking logic or database schema\\n- Changing the UI components for displaying achievements\\n- Adding achievements in other categories\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\n**R1: Category Addition**\\n- Add `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS = \\"famous_mustards\\"` to the AchievementCategory enum\\n\\n**R2: Achievement Definitions**\\n- Create exactly 10 new Achievement objects\\n- Each must reference famous mustard varieties (Dijon, Yellow, Honey Mustard, Spicy Brown, etc.)\\n- Names should be creative but clearly mustard-themed\\n- Descriptions should cleverly relate mustard characteristics to agent behaviors\\n- Must follow existing achievement patterns and structure\\n\\n**R3: Quality Standards**\\n- Achievements should have varied rarity levels (suggested: 3-4 common, 3-4 uncommon, 2-3 rare, 0-1 epic/legendary)\\n- Point values should align with rarity (10-15 common, 20-35 uncommon, 40-60 rare, 75+ epic/legendary)\\n- Icons should be food/mustard related emojis\\n- Trigger conditions should be realistic and achievable\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n\\n**T1: Code Integration**\\n- Achievements must be added to the existing ACHIEVEMENTS list in achievements.py\\n- Follow existing code structure and formatting\\n- No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n\\n**T2: Naming Conventions**\\n- Achievement IDs should follow snake_case pattern\\n- IDs should be descriptive and mustard-themed\\n- Names should be title case and engaging\\n\\n### Constraints\\n\\n**C1: System Compatibility**\\n- Must work with existing achievement tracking system\\n- Cannot modify database schema or core tracking logic\\n- Must use existing trigger condition patterns\\n\\n**C2: Theme Consistency**\\n- All achievements must be mustard-themed\\n- Should maintain the humorous, gaming-style tone of existing achievements\\n- Must fit naturally with the existing achievement ecosystem\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. \\u2705 10 new achievements added to the system\\n2. \\u2705 All achievements are mustard-themed and creative\\n3. \\u2705 Code integrates cleanly without breaking existing functionality\\n4. \\u2705 Achievements follow established patterns for structure and quality\\n5. \\u2705 Mixed rarity distribution provides progression incentives\\n6. \\u2705 Trigger conditions are realistic and varied\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- The existing achievement system architecture will not change\\n- The mustard theme should be applied broadly (types, brands, characteristics, uses)\\n- Achievements should maintain the existing humorous and gaming-inspired tone\\n- Standard software development practices will be followed\\n\\n## Technical Context\\n\\nThe system already has these achievement categories:\\n- SKA, BRASS_BAND, DRUM_CORPS, GUITAR_HERO (music-themed)\\n- PRODUCTIVITY, COMEDY, MILESTONE, STREAK, META (behavior-themed)\\n\\nThe new FAMOUS_MUSTARDS category will join this list and achievements will be added to the main ACHIEVEMENTS list in `/src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MbCH7hB82aasAD6fvT6Etp', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Fidget Spinner Achievements - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nAdd 10 new achievements from the "famous mustards" category to the existing achievement system in the ensemble project. This is a focused code enhancement that builds upon existing infrastructure without requiring UI or database changes.\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Foundation Setup (Phase 1)\n**Objective**: Establish the new FAMOUS_MUSTARDS category and prepare the codebase\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Add FAMOUS_MUSTARDS enum value to AchievementCategory\n- Research famous mustard varieties for achievement themes\n- Validate existing achievement system structure\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- FAMOUS_MUSTARDS category added to enum without breaking existing code\n- Code compiles and runs without errors\n- All existing achievements remain functional\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Estimated Duration**: 1 development cycle\n\n### Milestone 2: Achievement Design & Implementation (Phase 2) \n**Objective**: Create and implement all 10 mustard-themed achievements\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- 10 new Achievement objects with mustard themes\n- Varied rarity distribution (3-4 common, 3-4 uncommon, 2-3 rare, 0-1 epic/legendary)\n- Creative names and descriptions linking mustard characteristics to agent behaviors\n- Appropriate point values and trigger conditions\n- Mustard/food-related emoji icons\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All 10 achievements added to ACHIEVEMENTS list\n- Each achievement follows existing structure and patterns\n- Rarity and point values align with existing system standards\n- Trigger conditions are realistic and achievable\n- All achievements compile and integrate without errors\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\n**Estimated Duration**: 2 development cycles\n\n### Milestone 3: Testing & Quality Assurance (Phase 3)\n**Objective**: Verify system functionality and achievement quality\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Comprehensive test coverage for new achievements\n- Integration testing with existing achievement system\n- Code review and quality validation\n- Documentation updates if needed\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All tests pass without errors\n- New achievements trigger correctly in system\n- No regression issues with existing functionality\n- Code follows project standards and conventions\n- Achievement themes are creative and engaging\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 complete\n**Estimated Duration**: 1 development cycle\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n**Low Risk Items**:\n- Category enum addition (simple, non-breaking change)\n- Achievement object creation (follows established patterns)\n\n**Medium Risk Items**:\n- Theme creativity and quality (subjective, requires review)\n- Trigger condition realism (needs testing)\n\n**Mitigation Strategies**:\n- Follow existing achievement patterns closely\n- Test trigger conditions thoroughly\n- Review achievement themes for quality and humor\n\n## Resource Requirements\n\n**Technical Skills Needed**:\n- Python development\n- Understanding of existing achievement system\n- Test development and execution\n\n**Key Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/achievements.py` (primary modification)\n- Test files for achievement system\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n1. **Functionality**: All 10 achievements integrate without breaking existing system\n2. **Quality**: Achievements are creative, humorous, and thematically consistent\n3. **Standards**: Code follows project conventions and passes all tests\n4. **Integration**: New category works seamlessly with existing achievement tracking\n\n## Final Deliverables\n\nUpon project completion:\n- 10 new FAMOUS_MUSTARDS achievements in production system\n- Updated achievement category enum\n- Comprehensive test coverage\n- Clean, maintainable code following project standards'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MbCH7hB82aasAD6fvT6Etp', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_030238.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_030238.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed',