Create 10 new achievement definitions with:\\n  - Unique IDs related to mustard themes\\n  - Creative names referencing famous mustard types/brands\\n  - Descriptive text that ties mustard concepts to agent behaviors\\n  - Appropriate rarity levels (mix of common to legendary)\\n  - Relevant icons (mustard/food related emojis)\\n  - Point values consistent with existing system\\n  - Trigger conditions that make sense in context\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Modifying the achievement tracking logic or database schema\\n- Changing the UI components for displaying achievements\\n- Adding achievements in other categories\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\n**R1: Category Addition**\\n- Add `FAMOUS_MUSTARDS = \\"famous_mustards\\"` to the AchievementCategory enum\\n\\n**R2: Achievement Definitions**\\n- Create exactly 10 new Achievement objects\\n- Each must reference famous mustard varieties (Dijon, Yellow, Honey Mustard, Spicy Brown, etc.)\\n- Names should be creative but clearly mustard-themed\\n- Descriptions should cleverly relate mustard characteristics to agent behaviors\\n- Must follow existing achievement patterns and structure\\n\\n**R3: Quality Standards**\\n- Achievements should have varied rarity levels (suggested: 3-4 common, 3-4 uncommon, 2-3 rare, 0-1 epic/legendary)\\n- Point values should align with rarity (10-15 common, 20-35 uncommon, 40-60 rare, 75+ epic/legendary)\\n- Icons should be food/mustard related emojis\\n- Trigger conditions should be realistic and achievable\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n\\n**T1: Code Integration**\\n- Achievements must be added to the existing ACHIEVEMENTS list in achievements.py\\n- Follow existing code structure and formatting\\n- No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n\\n**T2: Naming Conventions**\\n- Achievement IDs should follow snake_case pattern\\n- IDs should be descriptive and mustard-themed\\n- Names should be title case and engaging\\n\\n### Constraints\\n\\n**C1: System Compatibility**\\n- Must work with existing achievement tracking system\\n- Cannot modify database schema or core tracking logic\\n- Must use existing trigger condition patterns\\n\\n**C2: Theme Consistency**\\n- All achievements must be mustard-themed\\n- Should maintain the humorous, gaming-style tone of existing achievements\\n- Must fit naturally with the existing achievement ecosystem\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. \\u2705 10 new achievements added to the system\\n2. \\u2705 All achievements are mustard-themed and creative\\n3. \\u2705 Code integrates cleanly without breaking existing functionality\\n4. \\u2705 Achievements follow established patterns for structure and quality\\n5. \\u2705 Mixed rarity distribution provides progression incentives\\n6. \\u2705 Trigger conditions are realistic and varied\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- The existing achievement system architecture will not change\\n- The mustard theme should be applied broadly (types, brands, characteristics, uses)\\n- Achievements should maintain the existing humorous and gaming-inspired tone\\n- Standard software development practices will be followed\\n\\n## Technical Context\\n\\nThe system already has these achievement categories:\\n- SKA, BRASS_BAND, DRUM_CORPS, GUITAR_HERO (music-themed)\\n- PRODUCTIVITY, COMEDY, MILESTONE, STREAK, META (behavior-themed)\\n\\nThe new FAMOUS_MUSTARDS category will join this list and achievements will be added to the main ACHIEVEMENTS list in `/src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UrRceoKT12wjBefyjCNk1B', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementToast.jsx'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UrRceoKT12wjBefyjCNk1B', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "File not found: /Users/mattbillock/Developme